irkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/commits/ddc673598fb4101f014887fc99d5594be2df1dd6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T18:23:33Z","email":"dirkwahrheit@gmail.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T05:47:25Z","email":"teppo.kurki@iki.fi","name":"Teppo Kurki"},"message":"docs(history): state that a position is a [longitude, latitude] pair\n\nThe OpenAPI schema for /history/values allows a number array in a data\ncell, with [-120.5, 59.2] in its example, and both signalk-to-influxdb2\nand signalk-parquet return navigation.position that way. The DataRow\ncomment said \"objects (like navigation.position)\" and the docs said\nnothing, so a provider written from them returned the data model''s\n{latitude, longitude} instead, and a client written to the schema read\nnothing. Say it in both places, with a position column in the example.","tree":{"sha":"75e64936d72b2a1127034fbc67c71173e45b884b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/git/trees/75e64936d72b2a1127034fbc67c71173e45b884b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/git/commits/ddc673598fb4101f014887fc99d5594be2df1dd6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1049678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tkurki","id":1049678,"login":"tkurki","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNDk2Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/signalk-server/commit/ddc673598fb4101f014887fc99d5594be2df1dd6","node_id":"C_kwDOAUuXCdoAKGRkYzY3MzU5OGZiNDEwMWYwMTQ4ODdmYzk5ZDU1OTRiZTJkZjFkZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/signalk-server/commit/dac6cc931d4b03f7ccb08dfe69f8f3d5c1e79980","sha":"dac6cc931d4b03f7ccb08dfe69f8f3d5c1e79980","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/commits/dac6cc931d4b03f7ccb08dfe69f8f3d5c1e79980"}],"sha":"ddc673598fb4101f014887fc99d5594be2df1dd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/commits/ddc673598fb4101f014887fc99d5594be2df1dd6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/commits/dac6cc931d4b03f7ccb08dfe69f8f3d5c1e79980/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T23:17:49Z","email":"dirkwahrheit@gmail.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T19:35:57Z","email":"teppo.kurki@iki.fi","name":"Teppo Kurki"},"message":"fix(plugin-ci): replace npm 10.9.x on Node 22 runners\n\nnpm 10.9.x crashes while resolving an optional peer that is not being\ninstalled:\n\n  npm error Cannot read properties of null (reading ''edgesOut'')\n      at #loadPeerSet (@npmcli/arborist/lib/arborist/build-ideal-tree.js)\n\nAny plugin depending on vitest reaches it through\n@vitest/browser-playwright, so every Node 22 job fails at install before\na single test runs, whatever the pull request changed. It is upstream\nnpm/cli#9960 and #9787, both still open, and it is deterministic — the\ninstall retry already in this workflow cannot clear it.\n\nBoth Node-setup jobs now replace that minor with npm 11. The version\ntest is an exact 10.9.* match rather than \"older than 11\": Node 20 ships\nnpm 10.8.2, which resolves the same tree cleanly, so upgrading it would\nbe churn that fixes nothing.\n\nThe range stops at 11 rather than tracking npm@latest. npm 12 requires\nNode ^22.22.2, and `npm install -g` enforces an engine range with a hard\nnotsup failure rather than a warning, so @latest would fail this step\noutright on a caller pinning an earlier 22.x — trading a crash that only\naffects vitest users for one that affects everyone. npm 11 needs only\n>=22.9.0 and fixes the crash. Within 11 the range floats, so patch\nreleases arrive without a change here.\n\nReplacing npm rather than dropping Node 22 from the matrix keeps the job\ntesting a runtime plugins are still installed on: the crash is npm''s,\nnot Node''s.","tree":{"sha":"e398f1ccaf673e46a892ebf9dded41fd8ab43757","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/git/trees/e398f1ccaf673e46a892ebf9dded41fd8ab43757"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/git/commits/dac6cc931d4b03f7ccb08dfe69f8f3d5c1e79980","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1049678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tkurki","id":1049678,"login":"tkurki","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNDk2Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/signalk-server/commit/dac6cc931d4b03f7ccb08dfe69f8f3d5c1e79980","node_id":"C_kwDOAUuXCdoAKGRhYzZjYzkzMWQ0YjAzZjdjY2IwOGRmZTY5ZjhmM2Q1YzFlNzk5ODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/signalk-server/commit/41087af2a9d01440d1327f228c0bc649a62d7ed7","sha":"41087af2a9d01440d1327f228c0bc649a62d7ed7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/commits/41087af2a9d01440d1327f228c0bc649a62d7ed7"}],"sha":"dac6cc931d4b03f7ccb08dfe69f8f3d5c1e79980","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Si