tiple IPs hitting that limit concurrently.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg9vmoave7dgcQGdCu26jzSUELxZ\nIbEj09nSzjU/MCuKwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQH/4DHFFVl+YnvAZndmVYnnUc2FtwBXDZS914/jhYmXrya3Q8ofMtr+NvzX1zs9xDS\nj/VAqnxaEPMWhdcQYhfAA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T20:31:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1049678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tkurki","id":1049678,"login":"tkurki","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNDk2Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/signalk-server/commit/cf8fceee43c1da73be8a5e654d72b5a01f054093","node_id":"C_kwDOAUuXCdoAKGNmOGZjZWVlNDNjMWRhNzNiZThhNWU2NTRkNzJiNWEwMWYwNTQwOTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/signalk-server/commit/8e045b747a082273703165260e2bcc6064b6d517","sha":"8e045b747a082273703165260e2bcc6064b6d517","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/commits/8e045b747a082273703165260e2bcc6064b6d517"}],"sha":"cf8fceee43c1da73be8a5e654d72b5a01f054093","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/commits/cf8fceee43c1da73be8a5e654d72b5a01f054093"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/commits/8e045b747a082273703165260e2bcc6064b6d517/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T18:38:02Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T18:38:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(plugin-ci): add working-directory input for monorepo plugins (#2990)\n\n* feat(plugin-ci): add working-directory input for monorepo plugins\n\nThe reusable plugin-ci workflow assumed the plugin sits at the\nrepository root: every step resolved package.json from the checkout\nroot, npm pack ran there, and the armv7 container used /plugin as its\nworkdir. A plugin published from a subdirectory — npm''s standard\n`repository.directory`, e.g. openwatersio/aiscast — therefore could not\nadopt the workflow at all, since the root manifest is either a\nworkspace shell or absent entirely.\n\nAdds a `working-directory` input defaulting to `.`, threaded through\n`defaults.run` on all four jobs so every run-step follows it without\ntouching each step individually. The cases defaults.run cannot reach\nare handled explicitly: the armv7 container''s `-w`, the artifact upload\npaths, the integration job''s absolute `github.workspace` manifest reads\n(those steps cd elsewhere first), and the ci-status sparse-checkout.\n\nThe sparse-checkout needs the conditional rather than plain\ninterpolation: a non-cone pattern of `./package.json` matches nothing,\nso the default would silently check out no files.\n\nExisting callers are unaffected — the default resolves to the same\npaths they use today.\n\n* fix(plugin-ci): select the manifest with an explicit non-cone pattern\n\n* fix(plugin-ci): pass working-directory through env, not interpolation\n\nCodeRabbit flagged command injection on the new input, and it was right.\nGitHub substitutes ${{ inputs.* }} into the script text before bash\nparses it, so double quotes give no protection: a caller passing\n`$(...)` or a backtick value executed arbitrary commands at the four\npackage.json lookups and the armv7 docker -w. Verified by rendering the\ngenerated script — the payload ran.\n\nThe workflow already had the answer: every other caller-controlled\ninput (build-command, test-command, coverage-command,\nformat-check-command) is passed via `env:` and referenced as a shell\nvariable. This change was the odd one out. All five shell sites now\nfollow that convention, and the two node -e lookups take the path as\nargv rather than splicing it into JavaScript source.\n\nThe remaining uses are YAML fields (defaults.run, artifact paths,\nsparse-checkout) where interpolation is not shell, but `..` and\nwildcards there could still broaden artifact and checkout matches, so a\nvalidate-inputs job gates the whole workflow on a plain relative path.\n\nThe single-line check is deliberate and not redundant: grep anchors\n^...$ per line, so a multi-line value passes the pattern check alone.\nThat case is now rejected, along with traversal, absolute and ~ paths,\nwildcards, quotes and substitutions.\n\nNot pinning actions/checkout to a SHA: all four checkout steps in this\nworkflow pin by major tag, and changing one of them here would be\ninconsistent and unrelated to this input.\n\n* fix(plugin-ci): fail the status report when input validation fails\n\n* fix(plugin-ci): satisfy prettier on the working-directory description\n\nPrettier''s YAML formatter prefers double quotes over doubled-single-quote\nescaping for a string containing an apostrophe. The description text is\nunchanged; only the quoting style differs.\n\nFixes the ci-lint failure on the build job.","tree":{"sha":"4278808dddb221986a6da26a5d40eec8eea440ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/git/trees/4278808dddb221986a6da26a5d40eec8eea440ce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/git/commits/8e045b747a082273703165260e2bcc6064b6d517","verification":{"payload":"tree 4278808dddb221986a6da26a5d40eec8eea440ce\nparent 257ccf98f2882d420bdd24c5a1568c33d5c6c35c\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1787769482 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787769482 +0300\n\nfeat(plugin-ci): add working-directory input for monorepo plugins (#2990)\n\n* feat(plugin-ci): add working-directory input for monorepo plugins\n\nThe reusable plugin-ci workflow assumed the plugin sits at the\nrepository root: every step resolved package.json from the checkout\nroot, npm pack ran there, and the armv7 container used /plugin as its\nworkdir. A plugin published from a subdirectory — npm''s standard\n`repository.directory`, e.g. openwatersio/aiscast — therefore could not\nadopt the workflow at all, since the root manifest is either a\nworkspace shell or absent entirely.\n\nAdds a `working-directory` input defaulting to `.`, threaded through\n`defaults.run` on all four jobs so every run-step follows it without\ntouching each step individually. The cases defaults.run cannot reach\nare handled explicitly: the armv7 container''s `-w`, the artifact upload\npaths, the integration job''s absolute `github.workspace` manifest reads\n(those steps cd elsewhere first), and the ci-status sparse-checkout.\n\nThe sparse-checkout needs the conditional rather than plain\ninterpolation: a non-cone pattern of `./package.json` matches nothing,\nso the default would silently check out no files.\n\nExisting callers are unaffected — the default resolves to the same\npaths they use today.\n\n* fix(plugin-ci): select the manifest with an explicit non-cone pattern\n\n* fix(plugin-ci): pass working-directory through env, not interpolation\n\nCodeRabbit flagged command injection on the new input, and it was right.\nGitHub substitutes ${{ inputs.* }} into the script text before bash\nparses it, so double quotes give no protection: a caller passing\n`$(...)` or a backtick value executed arbitrary commands at the four\npackage.json lookups and the armv7 docker -w. Verified by rendering the\ngenerated script — the payload ran.\n\nThe workflow already had the answer: every other caller-controlled\ninput (build-command, test-command, coverage-command,\nformat-check-command) is passed via `env:` and referenced as a shell\nvariable. This change was the odd one out. All five shell sites now\nfollow that convention, and the two node -e lookups take the path as\nargv rather than splicing it into JavaScript source.\n\nThe remaining uses are YAML fields (defaults.run, artifact paths,\nsparse-checkout) where interpolation is not shell, but `..` and\nwildcards there could still broaden artifact and checkout matches, so a\nvalidate-inputs job gates the whole workflow on a plain relative path.\n\nThe single-line check is deliberate and not redundant: grep anchors\n^...$ per line, so a multi-line value passes the pattern check alone.\nThat case is now rejected, along with traversal, absolute and ~ paths,\nwildcards, quotes and substitutions.\n\nNot pinning actions/checkout to a SHA: all four checkout steps in this\nworkflow pin by major tag, and changing one of them here would be\ninconsistent and unrelated to this input.\n\n* fix(plugin-ci): fail the status report when input validation fails\n\n* fix(plugin-ci): satisfy prettier on the working-directory description\n\nPrettier''s YAML formatter prefers double quotes over doubled-single-quote\nescaping for a string containing an apostrophe. The description text is\nunchanged; only the quoting style differs.\n\nFixes the ci-lint failure on the build job.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjzKKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6fAQABjcyPRcH4EMvbsrOld1yOmr\nyEkrehrFwas0/hSmLZc27xpP3LwBa8qXzcuAkgkyxSox5oilCkAb6Mbm5hyHiRIm\n2flAB5UI2X+8fBqNVVioZtxd/xXxJ1P2DLFQtqMZEhUOT21gwtZEWWEco+pnFwOY\nEjum4tz0nhVXWlYhgoSNSvj1bsuSPzzeWQmE+GodfOvPDCGBshigghqI3uiChyRQ\nuQSE7Mxmkf3nozzVEivBgIf8BgmC9/CeE0HvUjmf5Kuwm+p4O+2o5cZ+v1JRymw8\nCSLe0++Ky4JklXacx2gSbkDxRMdwj713txXunfE5D+CiPwhbA83ya87tz0XeNUHq\nrKgsOVSiVgXr/cRqDt+zmEAIwlZSYGaaFPHHYDrWK9/+lKmA6Y1JsTyQhLHDKVTW\nlo9yFyKfK0qlXmScLb0P7bJR3LO1f/RgAXNODT4C0YIn58QJJdQ90jcX1Tb8doW9\nHnLVqs0vO4ScdxhMN7u6gg/hmORMmxFoE0TnClsWGk6875QrWvy//NFVUJ9iVesB\ncEjuTKF2gO+uHXNoSUpEV2JGeWO32hF9WBznHRqn2ITgSZzn6ViQpkvwjbsO9oad\nhtWjuCPvTTcysIpPXU8V01ocInrRE8e8UlGlMte5oq+E+2rscjPGgYHyLZQXPOeQ\ntqluFveutZEL04LLrPj9\n=iKpe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T18:38:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/signalk-server/commit/8e045b747a082273703165260e2bcc6064b6d517","node_id":"C_kwDOAUuXCdoAKDhlMDQ1Yjc0N2EwODIyNzM3MDMxNjUyNjBlMmJjYzYwNjRiNmQ1MTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/signalk-server/commit/257ccf98f2882d420bdd24c5a1568c33d5c6c35c","sha":"257ccf98f2882d420bdd24c5a1568c33d5c6c35c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/commits/257ccf98f2882d420bdd24c5a1568c33d5c6c35c"}],"sha":"8e045b747a082273703165260e2bcc6064b6d517","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/commits/8e045b747a082273703165260e2bcc6064b6d517"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/commits/257ccf98f2882d420bdd24c5a1568c33d5c6c35c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T05:53:20Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T05:53:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(admin-ui): forward a plugin''s whole schema to the configuration form (#2994)\n\n* fix(admin-ui): forward a plugin''s whole schema to the form\n\nThe plugin configuration form rebuilt its schema by copying two named fields\noff `plugin.schema`:\n\n  description: plugin.schema.description,\n  properties: plugin.schema.properties\n\nEverything else was silently dropped — `dependencies`, `oneOf`, `allOf`,\n`required`. A plugin that made one field conditional on another therefore got\na field that rendered in NO state at all, rather than in one of them, and the\ncontrolling toggle appeared to do nothing.\n\nFound in signalk-tailscale 1.0.2, which used `dependencies` to hide a\n\"self-hosted URL\" field while the container is managed. The field vanished\nentirely and the URL became unconfigurable; that release had to be reverted.\n\nSpread the schema instead, keeping the explicit `type`/`title` overrides the\nform needs. RJSF resolves a nested object field''s `dependencies` against that\nobject''s own form data at render time, so the conditional then behaves.\n\nPluginSchema gains an index signature — a plugin''s schema is arbitrary JSON\nSchema, and the two named members are only those read directly here.","tree":{"sha":"c574daf36bf987b3c7a643718ec89cc2fe6e147d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/git/trees/c574daf36bf987b3c7a643718ec89cc2fe6e147d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/git/commits/257ccf98f2882d420bdd24c5a1568c33d5c6c35c","verification":{"payload":"tree c574daf36bf987b3c7a643718ec89cc2fe6e147d\nparent e7dd77059020c927162fdcde6f16fb01da197413\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1787723600 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787723600 +0300\n\nfix(admin-ui): forward a plugin''s whole schema to the configuration form (#2994)\n\n* fix(admin-ui): forward a plugin''s whole schema to the form\n\nThe plugin configuration form rebuilt its schema by copying two named fields\noff `plugin.schema`:\n\n  description: plugin.schema.description,\n  properties: plugin.schema.properties\n\nEverything else was silently dropped — `dependencies`, `oneOf`, `allOf`,\n`required`. A plugin that made one field conditional on another therefore got\na field that rendered in NO state at all, rather than in one of them, and the\ncontrolling toggle appeared to do nothing.\n\nFound in signalk-tailscale 1.0.2, which used `dependencies` to hide a\n\"self-hosted URL\" field while the container is managed. The field vanished\nentirely and the URL became unconfigurable; that release had to be reverted.\n\nSpread the schema instead, keeping the explicit `type`/`title` overrides the\nform needs. RJSF resolves a nested object field''s `dependencies` against that\nobject''s own form data at render time, so the conditional then behaves.\n\nPluginSchema gains an index signature — a plugin''s schema is arbitrary JSON\nSchema, and the two named members are only those read directly here.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjn9QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkjwQAJ/ehkVOn+9zhSLvI+CWjFsQ\neLsGf3yyER7ATdpK9OjdNbkJwX4juhEqAl6cB0Q67bodUElNsuDupvprI6vrD5Se\nBTXW6VW2BOh+OAEcyGzsdz7/7FZYJJKCUE9K9uIfWfAEJIIpF5v6DUdXhix+9q2s\nvbORymWtXg6nnUZrOfslGnOK/vLupd9s7ywfqYaUFHI//X3EeQgTX20i845S9fQJ\n4MVsafhotYX7R7Jz3PtsV1XqbN4uX++Ny6mzmoUFKPsO9nb1ckILxsZ91RmIIieH\nNDDtii6JAiGuA10OCmeKkdC9c5vL5WILH8N6wqh8AeFXeS9DKxIh++6OFHFlneES\nxX145cFoMRCIvjYoEvz34AokH7qI17TpABU4eHYseqJqOGdh2Dw4Ea0GWrA9VaWX\n7y5J58BIva5gpp6iS2g/FC0aMCDRM1yxm9zCmTrXDY6QTLkZQxN2wq/Uix9OdC4X\nHbTdNBTbg4GEP297g7zr0PRTbOLGoR/fqW3SnEeGqTRWfXkNdlXxZJzIZWXLnTeF\nAcA9p5MMwCgjPVKFckzSunze/SXS09qD4ELOy6iveTpGPATBespqYkKCHdnb1tY/\nS0uomteec2SecmNBFY1G95ciytZeTSjFDMNOIDuWHCK0XBHlR54MPOEVQYfCzvd7\noWAq6+dtI1jUMRjWyDZW\n=nk/K\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T05:53:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/signalk-server/commit/257ccf98f2882d420bdd24c5a1568c33d5c6c35c","node_id":"C_kwDOAUuXCdoAKDI1N2NjZjk4ZjI4ODJkNDIwYmRkMjRjNWExNTY4YzMzZDVjNmMzNWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/signalk-server/commit/e7dd77059020c927162fdcde6f16fb01da197413","sha":"e7dd77059020c927162fdcde6f16fb01da197413","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/commits/e7dd77059020c927162fdcde6f16fb01da197413"}],"sha":"257ccf98f2882d420bdd24c5a1568c33d5c6c35c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/commits/257ccf98f2882d420bdd24c5a1568c33d5c6c35c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/407010?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mairas","id":407010,"login":"mairas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzAxMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/commits/e7dd77059020c927162fdcde6f16fb01da197413/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T10:40:37Z","email":"matti.airas@hatlabs.fi","name":"Matti Airas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T04:29:02Z","email":"teppo.kurki@iki.fi","name":"Teppo Kurki"},"message":"fix(config): track whether settings are safe to persist\n\napp.config.settings does not always hold what the user configured.\n--data disables every configured pipedProvider and adds a FileStream\nfor the log, the sample data flags add providers, and a settings file\nthat exists but cannot be parsed falls back to empty settings. Writers\nthat serialise that object save the stand-in over the real file, and\nthe next ordinary start reads it back as the user''s own configuration.\n\nThe sourceRef migration is such a writer and needs no user action: it\nruns ten seconds after a device changes bus address. Replaying an N2K\nlog with --data is enough to save a settings.json with every real\nconnection disabled.\n\nRecord the state in config.safeToPersistSettings and skip both of the\nmigration''s writes while it is cleared, settings.json and the channel\nlabels file, so a run either persists the whole rename or none of it.\nThe rewrites still apply in memory, so the running server is\nconsistent with itself. The skip is permanent rather than deferred:\nmigration runs from the sourceRefChanged event, and a later start of a\ndevice already at its new address raises no such event, so the log\nline names both refs for a manual rename.\n\nA missing settings file does not clear the flag; there is nothing to\noverwrite and a fresh install must still be able to save.\n\nThis does not make settings safe in general. Every writer serialises\nthe whole object, so the admin UI and ResourcesApi.saveSettings can\nstill persist a replaced connection list. Those paths need their own\nfix.","tree":{"sha":"b6ffd16d60181f3d1e0fe69074d692809a4b5755","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/git/trees/b6ffd16d60181f3d1e0fe69074d692809a4b5755"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/git/commits/e7dd77059020c927162fdcde6f16fb01da197413","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1049678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tkurki","id":1049678,"login":"tkurki","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNDk2Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tkurki","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/signalk-server/commit/e7dd77059020c927162fdcde6f16fb01da197413","node_id":"C_kwDOAUuXCdoAKGU3ZGQ3NzA1OTAyMGM5MjcxNjJmZGNkZTZmMTZmYjAxZGExOTc0MTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/signalk-server/commit/145fa7a1f6f5081fb8a68d4262c33514e97aba70","sha":"145fa7a1f6f5081fb8a68d4262c33514e97aba70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/commits/145fa7a1f6f5081fb8a68d4262c33514e97aba70"}],"sha":"e7dd77059020c927162fdcde6f16fb01da197413","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/commits/e7dd77059020c927162fdcde6f16fb01da197413"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/commits/145fa7a1f6f5081fb8a68d4262c33514e97aba70/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T04:11:03Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T04:11:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(plugins): expose unregisterHistoryApiProvider to plugins (#2997)\n\n* fix(plugins): expose unregisterHistoryApiProvider to plugins\n\nFixes #2996\n\n`HistoryProviderRegistry` declares `unregisterHistoryApiProvider()`, and\n`ServerAPI` extends it, so the method is part of the typed surface a\nplugin sees and TypeScript accepts the call. The server never assigned\nit: only the register half was placed on the app copy, and the sole call\nto the registry method lived inside the plugin''s own stop handler. A\nplugin calling it got a TypeError at a type-clean call site.\n\nStopping a plugin already unregisters its provider, so the common path\nwas unaffected. What was missing is withdrawing while staying loaded —\na provider that has lost its backing store would rather deregister than\nanswer queries it cannot serve.\n\nThe registry ignores an unknown plugin id, so the stop handler firing\nafter a manual unregister is a no-op and needs no guard.\n\nThe demo plugin test now asserts both halves are present on the app a\nplugin receives. Verified it fails without the fix.\n\n* test: move the provider registry assertions to TypeScript\n\nNew test code in this repo is TypeScript — 33 of the last 34 test files\nadded are .ts — so the assertions move out of the legacy plugins.js into\ntheir own file rather than adding JavaScript to it. plugins.js is left\nuntouched.\n\nThe withdrawal test asserts against the registry rather than\ngetHistoryApi(). Other plugins in the test config register history\nproviders too, so the API still resolves through one of those after\ntestplugin withdraws, and asserting on it would have passed whether or\nnot the provider actually left.\n\nVerified both tests fail without the fix: the first on the explicit\nassertion, the second with the TypeError a plugin would hit.\n\n* test: leave plugins.js untouched\n\nThe assertions live in plugin-provider-registry.ts now; this reverts the\nJavaScript ones so the legacy file is unchanged by this PR.\n\n* test: restore SIGNALK_NODE_CONFIG_DIR and name the timeout\n\nMocha runs every test file in one process, so leaving the config dir set\npointed whatever ran next at the plugin fixtures. Captured and restored\nthe same way history-api.ts does, deleting the key when it was unset.\n\nThe repeated 30s literal becomes a named constant.","tree":{"sha":"6672f95319504005e667e6fe5ff5c3101e3e1302","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/git/trees/6672f95319504005e667e6fe5ff5c3101e3e1302"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-server/git/commits/145fa7a1f6f5081fb8a68d4262c33514e97aba70","verification":{"payload":"tree 6672f95319504005e667e6fe5ff5c3101e3e1302\nparent 9edfbf958eb7addb69140a605b4d21a0df249fdc\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1787717463 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787717463 +0300\n\nfix(plugins): expose unregisterHistoryApiProvider to plugins (#2997)\n\n* fix(plugins): expose unregisterHistoryApiProvider to plugins\n\nFixes #2996\n\n`HistoryProviderRegistry` declares `unregisterHistoryApiProvider()`, and\n`ServerAPI` extends it, so the method is part of the typed surface a\nplugin sees and TypeScript accepts the call. The server never assigned\nit: only the register half was placed on the app copy, and the sole call\nto the registry method lived inside the plugin''s own stop handler. A\nplugin calling it got a TypeError at a type-clean call site.\n\nStopping a plugin already unregisters its provider, so the common path\nwas unaffected. What was missing is withdrawing while staying loaded —\na provider that has lost its backing store would rather deregister than\nanswer queries it cannot serve.\n\nThe registry ignores an unknown plugin id, so the stop handler firing\nafter a manual unregister is a no-op and needs no guard.\n\nThe demo plugin test now asserts both halves are present on the app a\nplugin receives. Verified it fails without the fix.\n\n* test: move the provider registry assertions to TypeScript\n\nNew test code in this repo is TypeScript — 33 of the last 34 test files\nadded are .ts — so the assertions move out of the legacy plugins.js into\ntheir own file rather than adding JavaScript to it. plugins.js is left\nuntouched.\n\nThe withdrawal test asserts against the registry rather than\ngetHistoryApi(). Other plugins in the test config register history\nproviders too, so the API still resolves through one of those after\ntestplugin withdraws, and asserting on it would have passed whether or\nnot the provider actually left.\n\nVerified both tests fail without the fix: the first on the explicit\nassertion, the second with the TypeError a plugin would hit.\n\n* test: leave plugins.js untouched\n\nThe assertions live in plugin-provider-registry.ts now; this reverts the\nJavaScript ones so the legacy file is unchanged by this PR.\n\n* test: restore SIGNALK_NODE_CONFIG_DIR and name the timeout\n\nMocha runs every test file in one process, so leaving the config dir set\npointed whatever ran next at the plugin fixtures. Captured and restored\nthe same way history-api.ts does, deleting the key when it was unset.\n\nThe repeated 30s literal becomes a named constant.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjmdXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATlUQAAtSzxOmGvx9NCtN94YpdjsJ\nIjWcWbT//8v5NQ6DYPNH+QDvr5x6L0fHcX9b3PqhNZ89ko+Ljbv5sqzv9BTYhSJL\nILuMD9qE7zylJgydTVGp+7Ke3ahcNl0NAs9FhjC5haFxk1jsYyN91ri8XSLnMzGM\na42HPrLdDxq9V4uAvBM5/s9LCpz1cIdY+Y7gygdm8NdTO0+tSjkcoj2yx2DdlK2O\nl8/QJ/Pj+RCevELsArtimyoSeczC8KajNnGOrFFvuz7uvP+0XDxgjaQAPg7t+xvQ\n3CJCs++YdHdV3vfGi/xIW0rDqIIpMP95Gayc4Nu/quw0Dg9L+6GXvRzhv7wv53SH\n0wEImTZSOIyfetbt903wtsVxh/4mm53LlDlEjye4z255qL0fhU8GdNrZ6D82GOgc\nCGyGPhvjeA+jfLAcjg1oRjeW7J3DCJnGvYUkN/HTyIfrgWq0hF/ynju1oy8m92A9\nuAY80pFJTS1Dx81m8GgmhnfszHb9E7mvw3i9/S2RX4R+0cqXeEt56pq7ECXz35LG\ntjHg/8vDT9r3SquwgmHHfJXA7TlRqAp095DaT7hRnLT+Zi9zQvmZJXpnGtxwCICT\nUckg4T90C6LviTrpPzr9x/4aYIwu7c4rry3aRU0i707K296Wo/F4fmNipnSj9tck\nLjtZCadpewEujeurvZZT\n=h3g1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T04:11:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://