hub.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/ee80f57b258f205af5a10885804ea9b7382a5107/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T02:27:58Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T02:27:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(server): the shell is never cached, and built files are sent compressed (#475)\n\nA release broke the site for anyone who had visited in the last day.\nindex.html was cached for that long, so the browser kept a shell naming\nthe previous build''s files. Those were gone, and the server answered a\nmissing file with the shell and a 200, so the browser got HTML where it\nexpected a script.\n\nindex.html is now no-cache, on / and on every route that falls back to\nit. A missing file under /assets answers 404. The hashed files under\n/assets are immutable for a year; files with a fixed name keep a day.\n\nThe JavaScript was also sent uncompressed: compression() was registered\nafter the handlers that send files, so it never ran. The build now\nwrites a .gz and a .br beside each text file with\nvite-plugin-compression2, and a small middleware sends the one the\nbrowser accepts. compression() moves first and covers what is not a\nbuilt file: the shell and the API''s answers through the proxy.\n\nThe largest chunk goes from 2,236 KB to 615 KB with Brotli.\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <hello@ki-cl.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d849e2fdd00460951ca6ad06b1aca0e7f47964ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/trees/d849e2fdd00460951ca6ad06b1aca0e7f47964ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/commits/ee80f57b258f205af5a10885804ea9b7382a5107","verification":{"payload":"tree d849e2fdd00460951ca6ad06b1aca0e7f47964ec\nparent 1c692d7afe0a9c238b5a1c8903ac3c57ecb9023a\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1791426478 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791426478 -0700\n\nfix(server): the shell is never cached, and built files are sent compressed (#475)\n\nA release broke the site for anyone who had visited in the last day.\nindex.html was cached for that long, so the browser kept a shell naming\nthe previous build''s files. Those were gone, and the server answered a\nmissing file with the shell and a 200, so the browser got HTML where it\nexpected a script.\n\nindex.html is now no-cache, on / and on every route that falls back to\nit. A missing file under /assets answers 404. The hashed files under\n/assets are immutable for a year; files with a fixed name keep a day.\n\nThe JavaScript was also sent uncompressed: compression() was registered\nafter the handlers that send files, so it never ran. The build now\nwrites a .gz and a .br beside each text file with\nvite-plugin-compression2, and a small middleware sends the one the\nbrowser accepts. compression() moves first and covers what is not a\nbuilt file: the shell and the API''s answers through the proxy.\n\nThe largest chunk goes from 2,236 KB to 615 KB with Brotli.\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <hello@ki-cl.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxv+uCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbk8QADE8AbRg1J/dNE4WlybABEcn\nI29qGL8FZQxKfZ5vMM2m3e7/xK4ulm8rTguNnojhxcs0/7l2lV31qw1dQeSXcDfS\n1pngdLFUpGhfBo9UCdQra+c/WkT3XaDuxoMVvEI4ny+m9zm9l2HSuM5LSKG8gNaJ\nQCQCqPjMlJLuUxN/kdSuBC9tcJM8PSCiDz3e3WIdWGpTXLkrH7etUSP/SGAacXqb\nV4MDrjPpRaCy1SzBJ7oFf0kB2tdiWTN3LLl8uK1cV1YJemej934NPxSwNx26M+q9\npHoB+nvFiL9DlGZDWOxR3fXtbWrBOFheubH9I/w6YW/7QxOodEbeqR/WMpUgQkmo\nByKft9ScCqsD3Tvco6vn8E/SemFfNKROZLunHTfEDbce6UnXn3ntIWCBsWyAQk64\nBIpvIzGdboSoGN3f/DPtnNOVh/LcY5I7hrH7Csa+2j7eTK/562/MvXPaC5p6gU3+\n0We5iSGgykb1H0ESF4yMvWdkDGTOWRddouj1MfaOQuSrNNJOjABMftfOPvsDRoMB\nShoGbSz