8117fcc5adf8e17"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/kenilam/Ki.CL/commit/1c692d7afe0a9c238b5a1c8903ac3c57ecb9023a","sha":"1c692d7afe0a9c238b5a1c8903ac3c57ecb9023a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/1c692d7afe0a9c238b5a1c8903ac3c57ecb9023a"}],"sha":"bac6da4d807ec3e1c767b2e3bebb23316a7a953b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/bac6da4d807ec3e1c767b2e3bebb23316a7a953b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/1c692d7afe0a9c238b5a1c8903ac3c57ecb9023a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T01:04:11Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T01:04:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: async/await in place of promise chains, and a lazy sign-out dialog in the page shell (#473)\n\n* refactor: async/await in place of .then, and a lazy sign-out dialog in the page shell\n\nEvery lazy import and the five other .then chains (the session exchanges,\nloading Turnstile, the music visualiser''s copy link and audio resume) now\nuse async/await. CLAUDE.md shows the new form for lazy imports.\n\nThe sign-out dialog moves from the navigation to the page shell, after\nthe route''s Outlet, and its code is loaded only once someone is signed\nin. SignOut decides that itself, so the shell and the navigation no\nlonger ask who is signed in for it.\n\nThe copy-link button returns early when navigator.clipboard is missing.\nWith await it would otherwise have said \"copied\" without copying.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: try/catch in place of the remaining .catch and .finally\n\nThe seven standalone .catch(() => undefined) and .finally() calls now use\ntry/catch: the proxy''s token middleware, the analytics flush, the store\nreset after a session ends, the share sheet, the password confirm and\nthe portfolio gate''s refetch.\n\nThe proxy middleware awaits the mints and then calls next. mintIdToken\nnever rejects, so it needs no finally.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <hello@ki-cl.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"facb8932e825f324747a14da4bb35fa50fc1b397","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/trees/facb8932e825f324747a14da4bb35fa50fc1b397"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/commits/1c692d7afe0a9c238b5a1c8903ac3c57ecb9023a","verification":{"payload":"tree facb8932e825f324747a14da4bb35fa50fc1b397\nparent 721e66f7d92253058b7ccf7637c476c1b218ee21\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1791421451 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791421451 -0700\n\nrefactor: async/await in place of promise chains, and a lazy sign-out dialog in the page shell (#473)\n\n* refactor: async/await in place of .then, and a lazy sign-out dialog in the page shell\n\nEvery lazy import and the five other .then chains (the session exchanges,\nloading Turnstile, the music visualiser''s copy link and audio resume) now\nuse async/await. CLAUDE.md shows the new form for lazy imports.\n\nThe sign-out dialog moves from the navigation to the page shell, after\nthe route''s Outlet, and its code is loaded only once someone is signed\nin. SignOut decides that itself, so the shell and the navigation no\nlonger ask who is signed in for it.\n\nThe copy-link button returns early when navigator.clipboard is missing.\nWith await it would otherwise have said \"copied\" without copying.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: try/catch in place of the remaining .catch and .finally\n\nThe seven standalone .catch(() => undefined) and .finally() calls now use\ntry/catch: the proxy''s token middleware, the analytics flush, the store\nreset after a session ends, the share sheet, the password confirm and\nthe portfolio gate''s refetch.\n\nThe proxy middleware awaits the mints and then calls next. mintIdToken\nnever rejects, so it needs no finally.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <hello@ki-cl.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxuwLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACMYQAKQaHEsHu7qPlSyTzfED/UP/\nveEQz3hD3x+R/oV5SILA/IQvKud+6iVhtrgn8HSCTHATRCtRc4EbTyjZRyXKx/sD\njjVU7IXeSxfg3OAelbYiK817A9gAVBBMACrxEo04KVuj6YfYq/gtxSiXcdNP19Ky\nmmKFQcdWggoicrgfPzXRAkCO9anxjRjCQci37tYq8e1MW3c8mBhFDAl4NLIbFE52\nX41WfsmFYmXkb5m/tbj1t8PVnWSOr9ZFOi3nbpchZ5QdXfxpQokxWTV99c2Mhj0G\nT1EtjsF+IuesmahA1zGQon+XfmuPCBQk0yc073PfbWyec/Iip27X6MecjmeyohJ+\nU3Q1LWtxXLosFb6UFOLkeTm8cxk6Bv+c2VnZ2lmXFdk4WTf9NDrQ9ZPt/0SfA/HC\nhhURHCHVCQVqtozwLYeUzdWhDyq3Vkv6bnzqeRnarR4+lvVWtvwQ67x95y