nge such as an env var\nor secret only lands in the source region. gcp/region.sh copies the live\nservices across with the second region''s subnet and service URLs, and\nadds that region''s deploy step to the triggers if it''s missing.\n\nProject and resource names live in gcp/.env, which git ignores.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3b697ba80b7421545cfbb0910771ae53fd854b37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/trees/3b697ba80b7421545cfbb0910771ae53fd854b37"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/commits/fda3c81afd57fc0b7f85c234917e74bab184f676","verification":{"payload":"tree 3b697ba80b7421545cfbb0910771ae53fd854b37\nparent b1b3ede2660aa50867c5d1c4ae513456fc1dd9c8\nauthor Keni <657845+kenilam@users.noreply.github.com> 1791161927 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791161927 -0700\n\nfeat(gcp): make gcp.region copies production into the second region (#456)\n\nProduction runs in two regions behind a load balancer. The main triggers\ndeploy the same image to both, but a settings change such as an env var\nor secret only lands in the source region. gcp/region.sh copies the live\nservices across with the second region''s subnet and service URLs, and\nadds that region''s deploy step to the triggers if it''s missing.\n\nProject and resource names live in gcp/.env, which git ignores.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwvZHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzi4QAGpPcSD+hI5pEKfh7NA0ko4W\nhCi0e52xsMmwrV0jRucRomrJgSrxc0327zGWYKUYtq1RNG0aBS4eqa4BnprqfUa+\nCBhamfOeUV3iNCNzPGDAXGjaXhPCyfG4Zm8JoH/1nnh2dHPw4Wi+Wf09kpdBWwcW\nWiC+cItxG+XAZZRDCUFXaADIBqY59lQf5Wyx9Au61/fOMbpIzWcCLJjewsOdCm6d\nzKPT7/ESXd1kiRI4JciEElTn/5XXPcdS1aIhIF2fGwEfFFs7R5TsJxvxJseGdR5S\nQ929dD4UGSsItcrtbsQ/OFE3V3X8t7RFo9mRoJsdF7Jb08ytaeJQSijWTW6JjDGa\n/lJ7yqXpVSEYwiRgIWOqNjwIgZs8Fp0rBlV2ltMdKfIlwaspR/1MYo4qZCzAyZhe\nd8kb2gcO7q9nP2yIDg+dIDSLQ4pofCf