m/users/kenilam/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kenilam","id":657845,"login":"kenilam","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1Nzg0NQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/45b8b86478d42e595ecffefc61e54c391fe8ee05/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:32:26Z","email":"657845+kenilam@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Keni"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:32:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(styles): views use native CSS instead of the core Sass partials (#443)\n\nViews compiled the core partials in at build time (breakpoints, colours,\nscrim, stuck-line), which a federated design system can''t provide. They\nnow read what the core stylesheet already ships at runtime:\n\n- Breakpoints: core sets --kicl-viewport-{name} and\n  --kicl-viewport-up-to-{name} flags on :root, and views read them with\n  @container style() queries.\n- scrim and stuck-line are utility classes (kicl-scrim,\n  kicl-stuck-line-start/end) instead of mixins. Sheet uses them too.\n- The home background and music-visualiser inks are mixed in the browser\n  with color-mix() and relative hsl() from the --kicl-color-* tokens, and\n  registered as <color> with @property.\n\nThe browser computes those inks as oklab(), which a 2D context doesn''t read\nback as #rrggbb, so both palette readers now paint one pixel and read it\nwith getImageData.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bdd0b49367639c5d92e75561fca0cd159bb1d01e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/trees/bdd0b49367639c5d92e75561fca0cd159bb1d01e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/commits/45b8b86478d42e595ecffefc61e54c391fe8ee05","verification":{"payload":"tree bdd0b49367639c5d92e75561fca0cd159bb1d01e\nparent e76c43ba4d2ecffb7e1a7f768b08acac07259c7a\nauthor Keni <657845+kenilam@users.noreply.github.com> 1791066746 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791066746 -0700\n\nrefactor(styles): views use native CSS instead of the core Sass partials (#443)\n\nViews compiled the core partials in at build time (breakpoints, colours,\nscrim, stuck-line), which a federated design system can''t provide. They\nnow read what the core stylesheet already ships at runtime:\n\n- Breakpoints: core sets --kicl-viewport-{name} and\n  --kicl-viewport-up-to-{name} flags on :root, and views read them with\n  @container style() queries.\n- scrim and stuck-line are utility classes (kicl-scrim,\n  kicl-stuck-line-start/end) instead of mixins. Sheet uses them too.\n- The home background and music-visualiser inks are mixed in the browser\n  with color-mix() and relative hsl() from the --kicl-color-* tokens, and\n  registered as <color> with @property.\n\nThe browser computes those inks as oklab(), which a 2D context doesn''t read\nback as #rrggbb, so both palette readers now paint one pixel and read it\nwith getImageData.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwYJ6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMUQQAFsbIBldaMdJlZp9iM2BJgdk\n407nleJ4IgffKcSaFjiZeHSFzKI+Omip3DS3oT02UvTgqwxi72w/2O4fTMTmEJI7\nG8rKPBFtX7GPIb2sXTczSWGo2qtN/ItKL/9IJBQedqzCVQIFT5lmLlpWdQDDjCkY\nEXtCajhGJT+fgr0jV/uRtWAfsn1CkwM9gJWTTXBxVYsQOeeKYZkrdv3KkRV86Mos\nDNM26m3XdzpvlQAhhK+BV5vQ6/aa8A9QBarkdEaPvpY1itd1nNzgf1ip9vq+OcYl\nOjO1smqDshiHW6xIO13IMWjbODG0Ty+hHyeQt+RvgPPjaDy0EB3ItJebxi