.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/dc2477d5d2ca23241b7e771191669e82bbad6d21/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:47:02Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:47:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): get install and lint passing again on develop (#426)\n\n* refactor(styles): rank wrapper components with a cascade layer, not doubled selectors\n\nAnimation, Frame and InfiniteScroll clone their class onto another\ncomponent''s element, so both components'' rules land on one node at one\nclass each. In the same layer that is a tie, and the wrapper''s\ntransition or sizing won or lost by stylesheet order. Animation and\nFrame worked around it by matching their class twice. They now sit in a\n`wrappers` layer between `components` and `views`, and the doubling is\ngone.\n\nThe rest of the doubled selectors were left over from before layers\nexisted. The `make-variable-class` utilities and `kicl-backdrop` are in\n`utilities`, which already beats everything below, and the two view\n`__full` rules are in `views`, above the Dialog they override. Layout\nranked its own modifiers with doubled classes; they are in one file, so\nsource order does the same job.\n\nButton keeps its doubled selector. HyperLink with `lookLikeButton` puts\nboth classes on one anchor, and peers in one layer can only be ranked by\nspecificity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(deps): pin lint-staged back to 17.5.1 until 17.6.0 clears quarantine\n\nYarn 4.17 refuses any version published less than 24 hours ago, and\n17.6.0 came out this morning. Every branch off develop has failed at\n`yarn install --immutable` since #414 bumped it. 17.5.1 is 16 days old.\nRenovate will propose 17.6.0 again once it is old enough, now that it\nwaits a day (#425).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(oxlint): make the three React Compiler rules warnings for now\n\noxlint 1.85 (#415) added `react/refs`, `react/set-state-in-effect` and\n`react/purity` to the correctness category, and 38 places in the app\nfail them. That bump merged while CI could not get past install, so\nnobody saw it. They are warnings until the code is fixed, so CI reports\nthem without blocking every other change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <admin@loci.world>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d0e25303a79bd043979dd9f873fad4c9a175046c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/trees/d0e25303a79bd043979dd9f873fad4c9a175046c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/commits/dc2477d5d2ca23241b7e771191669e82bbad6d21","verification":{"payload":"tree d0e25303a79bd043979dd9f873fad4c9a175046c\nparent 072e63b498bddc85f9db3adb6d001e6d13d4fa32\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1790462822 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790462822 -0700\n\nfix(ci): get install and lint passing again on develop (#426)\n\n* refactor(styles): rank wrapper components with a cascade layer, not doubled selectors\n\nAnimation, Frame and InfiniteScroll clone their class onto another\ncomponent''s element, so both components'' rules land on one node at one\nclass each. In the same layer that is a tie, and the wrapper''s\ntransition or sizing won or lost by stylesheet order. Animation and\nFrame worked around it by matching their class twice. They now sit in a\n`wrappers` layer between `components` and `views`, and the doubling is\ngone.\n\nThe rest of the doubled selectors were left over from before layers\nexisted. The `make-variable-class` utilities and `kicl-backdrop` are in\n`utilities`, which already beats everything below, and the two view\n`__full` rules are in `views`, above the Dialog they override. Layout\nranked its own modifiers with doubled classes; they are in one file, so\nsource order does the same job.\n\nButton keeps its doubled selector. HyperLink with `lookLikeButton` puts\nboth classes on one anchor, and peers in one layer can only be ranked by\nspecificity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(deps): pin lint-staged back to 17.5.1 until 17.6.0 clears quarantine\n\nYarn 4.17 refuses any version published less than 24 hours ago, and\n17.6.0 came out this morning. Every branch off develop has failed at\n`yarn install --immutable` since #414 bumped it. 17.5.1 is 16 days old.\nRenovate will propose 17.6.0 again once it is old enough, now that it\nwaits a day (#425).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(oxlint): make the three React Compiler rules warnings for now\n\noxlint 1.85 (#415) added `react/refs`, `react/set-state-in-effect` and\n`react/purity` to the correctness category, and 38 places in the app\nfail them. That bump merged while CI could not get past install, so\nnobody saw it. They are warnings until the code is fixed, so CI reports\nthem without blocking every other change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <admin@loci.world>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquEtmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJnIQACRqWzCzRk/Sho4CZCB3Clsn\noRj4Izc9/gOkSJtj/ESeaVRnQAxlRSvjzfwHXUv/i00r26gQwgCjl5WAhE0Aly9g\nwszt/vVmVELUEjr41RxeZ1JEV92jGnHA6VHd7w330COGYsbIXBYZbtMQY/e+G7nK\nlALVbtrBfkJpSmKy1RUtz