he 16px floor\nis now !important.\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <admin@loci.world>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"73efce29242a06088be2589b21824aa33d0ebf76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/trees/73efce29242a06088be2589b21824aa33d0ebf76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/commits/7174d6931e3d3aa18856cba5cc85ae7ea6668ddc","verification":{"payload":"tree 73efce29242a06088be2589b21824aa33d0ebf76\nparent d40ea382c14af8e347be51434523f9392831aa1b\nauthor Keni <657845+kenilam@users.noreply.github.com> 1790280975 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790280975 -0700\n\nfeat(experiments): page dots, fewer wrappers, and a working iOS field zoom fix (#383)\n\nThe experiments index gets a column of dots on the right, one per plate,\nlinking to it. The current dot is a scroll-driven animation on the same\ntimeline as the plates, so there''s no scroll listener. It''s a new\nPageIndicator component so other paged views can use it.\n\nThe image agent composer and chat each lost a wrapper that only set the\n8-column width. The chat''s grid rows now apply to the header and\nconversation, and its content lines up with the composer.\n\nThe iOS zoom fix from #376 never applied: the kicl-font-size-* classes are\ndoubled for specificity, so they beat `:root :is(textarea)`. The 16px floor\nis now !important.\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <admin@loci.world>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtYUPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyRUQAHfpu1mnhYmhVTyHY0jfUtkV\nNLKY13EqoLcUPUk2SzdJlVLSNAg04RMSkt+jLTliRJsG0A/TgoeVem8asJ2rYuZE\nV89kYi30QqE/FoxeJaULTGmDZZaQJnjl2FqueEaB+FR5U9VpiE5c84dmfrmzAtTJ\nbxAae+h9rGryJp75rCocv7zGwwWIMJ8iWhcsh/hF+fFc/u9nh42mGiVYHiUW4Q+c\nmnmOi8xySdkrQ6sQhJyxeBK9+7y+eEjMTm+RoyXSK5244+1ZyVE0zsyFrdCxvDvK\nwZK7umwKomE2dQCtG9uZmf8bfq2zUL14SI4xSVcIEwq4S97A1ALAgOR/alXmqc1i\nc0ObTAaYZmnD+zdR