url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/a944519b564a48877190b667f69ac2b0f04f4819"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/657845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kenilam","id":657845,"login":"kenilam","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1Nzg0NQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/193fa31c1952e82afd3711b3998e90839ee19870/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T08:24:26Z","email":"657845+kenilam@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Keni"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T08:24:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Dev to Prod (#372)\n\n* fix(image-agent): richer backdrop and dark scrim in both themes\n\nThe pictures blended with plus-lighter, which added light and washed the\npreview out, and the scrim cut saturation on top. They now blend with\nsoft-light and the scrim keeps the colour. The hero and its home plate use\nthe dark theme in both modes, so the scrim darkens the picture and the text\nis white. The title no longer hardcodes white.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(experiments): fade each stage background in later\n\nThe next background was visible while the previous panel''s words were\nstill on screen. The fade now starts 0.3 of a screen before the panel\ninstead of 0.6.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(experiments): keep the scroll chevron from covering the hero content\n\nIt was absolutely positioned at the foot of the hero, so on small screens\nit sat on top of the text. It now follows the content.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <admin@loci.world>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ee5082a936f53e6c9bfc345c7ee3259b21ba4874","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/trees/ee5082a936f53e6c9bfc345c7ee3259b21ba4874"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/commits/193fa31c1952e82afd3711b3998e90839ee19870","verification":{"payload":"tree ee5082a936f53e6c9bfc345c7ee3259b21ba4874\nparent 16367e8a1eb2489626d593b9bec00adfd2823543\nauthor Keni <657845+kenilam@users.noreply.github.com> 1790238266 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790238266 -0700\n\nDev to Prod (#372)\n\n* fix(image-agent): richer backdrop and dark scrim in both themes\n\nThe pictures blended with plus-lighter, which added light and washed the\npreview out, and the scrim cut saturation on top. They now blend with\nsoft-light and the scrim keeps the colour. The hero and its home plate use\nthe dark theme in both modes, so the scrim darkens the picture and the text\nis white. The title no longer hardcodes white.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(experiments): fade each stage background in later\n\nThe next background was visible while the previous panel''s words were\nstill on screen. The fade now starts 0.3 of a screen before the panel\ninstead of 0.6.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(experiments): keep the scroll chevron from covering the hero content\n\nIt was absolutely positioned at the foot of the hero, so on small screens\nit sat on top of the text. It now follows the content.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <admin@loci.world>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtN46CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuBEQAFQHyBThA+8UflC40HzDTQUU\nf1viTXWvvXYE4W7hcesroqQTPLqo/kanDsz0+9rtaRFggthq7uxbmvguOS43IMO5\nE11vA3MLV2PdpGFnXGMUph0rpo2xigR/pv8eRncPNGCG2Hwwx7vznn63HYMQU7Df\nF00uYAeDIjbCjXMX2b+PMdXQ27DBaSuStuKVwrQT2LdwbiAwuLFjrflB/ZHtZIL0\nJQj7B/AaVnKRg+Mq5MgNpDILDUSZ0kc/a8itMOlT8dHkm/sP+wndikKW463iB7QW\n6p0hIh4C4UpmhmXjDv2YhhdiqsKoBcI4FrgNxqspf1IOSqONhjwWt4LYatZxnj10\n/obm6VJJ4ckwQX1k5ZKgHBB+vv5mGRZOdNvfV7MkgyupKw2/ULxVGikoLwRje7CC\nSd7UTYVFXh+YnjzQE9fRT60lmb0G8fyxL7AP9p4tDwnQ/HK0TMw3EwJt3QKFMJeb\nvQMI6ism6V3KQvRQjRlS/Ssw4llXl3Re1ymM1nMC2wexedUGczWp0EWA37OrbKUN\n+Gkvx+yFptISDCgsdqXzh2QfNxHDgaeWGcs7movXuAI0PTqwn9z8nANQXv9CDLc7\nZO9FT8CG1GdJ81GkaM8pzWb0EMHzdQ0jyUzBUvpcYjopUwoV3ibEu/gXRhyLkFTT\nrRfwSkBm5IkYIvJUJpqZ\n=R7Lz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T08:24:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kenilam/Ki.CL/commit/193fa31c1952e82afd3711b3998e90839ee19870","node_id":"C_kwDOAU3gWtoAKDE5M2ZhMzFjMTk1MmU4MmFmZDM3MTFiMzk5OGU5MDgzOWVlMTk4NzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kenilam/Ki.CL/commit/16367e8a1eb2489626d593b9bec00adfd2823543","sha":"16367e8a1eb2489626d593b9bec00adfd2823543","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/16367e8a1eb2489626d593b9bec00adfd2823543"}],"sha":"193fa31c1952e82afd3711b3998e90839ee19870","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/193fa31c1952e82afd3711b3998e90839ee19870"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/16367e8a1eb2489626d593b9bec00adfd2823543/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T07:42:01Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T07:42:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Dev to Prod (#371)\n\n* chore(deps): update dependency prettier to v3.9.8 (#367)\n\nrenovate updates\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat(components, core): Bubble, Combobox and a shared Diagram, plus column widths\n\nBubble and Combobox are new, for the image agent''s chat and composer. The\nPika diagram renderer moves to components/diagram so other pages can draw\ndiagrams, and gains a Legend. Layout takes a 12-column grid with span on\nits children, Card takes a column count as its size, and columns.scss\ndefines the widths. Scroll reveal, backdrop and the header''s gradient\nshift are now shared utilities.\n\nText resets its padding vars on each element. The sibling spacing used to\ninherit into any Text nested inside, so a legend after a paragraph drew\ntall chips with the value pushed down. The header keeps its last measured\nheight while hidden, and route focus compares paths so StrictMode''s\nsecond run doesn''t focus the page on load.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(portfolio): shared Diagram and tighter copy on the system design page\n\nThe page draws its diagrams with the shared Diagram component. The copy\ndrops pause dashes, colon punchlines and sentences that repeated the one\nbefore, and states each rule before walking through what happens.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(experiments): collapsible sections and plainer copy for the visualiser and tree of life\n\nThe music visualiser''s article sections are Details, like the tree of\nlife''s. Both articles refer to the reader in third person, and lose\nexplanations the reader doesn''t need.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(experiments): Image Agent\n\nA person describes a picture and an agent draws it, asking up to three\nquestions first if the description is too thin. The start page lists\nrunning and past conversations, and has a How it was made article. The\nchat follows one conversation over the ImageAgentThreadUpdated\nsubscription.\n\nOn the experiments home it is No. 3. Its plate is a mosaic of the\nbest-scored pictures, each shown once in the largest grid there are\nenough of them for. Two pictures stack over the whole plate with\nplus-lighter instead of splitting it. Each picture drifts inside its tile\non scroll.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: design system rules for column widths, launch configs and ignore .ua\n\nCLAUDE.md and the Cursor design system rule say widths come from the\n12-column scale. The launch configs cover the backend, the dev server and\na production preview.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(components): Frame, inline link icons, and card and dialog spacing\n\nFrame crops a full-screen view to the window less a gap, with rounded\ncorners. Its top follows the global header, which now publishes how much\nof the window it covers. It eases in from full-bleed by default, and hold\nkeeps a hero in place while it grows into the header''s space. Fixed\nchrome on a framed page clears the frame''s edge.\n\nLink icons flow inline with the text, so a closing arrow follows the\nlast word when it wraps, and the underline follows each line. Cards keep\ntheir padding on small screens, with more room at the foot. Dialogs and\nthe 404/500 pages take their widths from the column scale. The picture\nscrim is a shared mixin.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(image-agent): framed start page, shared backdrop and chat fixes\n\nThe start page is a framed hero with the title, how it works, the field\nand past conversations over the gallery backdrop. With no allowance\nleft, only past conversations show, and the badge stays. In a chat, a\nspent allowance also blocks rewinding and answering. The chat only\nscrolls to the end when the conversation is taller than the window. A\npicture opens full size from anywhere on it, titled after the\nconversation. Chat widths come from the column scale.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(views): frame every full-screen view\n\nThe home page, the experiments stage, the music visualiser and the tree\nof life sit in a Frame. On the stage, each panel''s picture tucks into\nthe frame as it arrives and the words can pass its edge; the Image\nAgent plate uses the shared backdrop, every picture once. The music\nvisualiser and tree of life heroes hold while the frame grows. On the\nhome page the frame eases in before the content. Widths that were\nhand-set now come from the column scale.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(portfolio): column widths for the system design page\n\nThe article body and the fullscreen diagrams use the column scale\ninstead of hand-set widths.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <admin@loci.world>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e90de29412689da23c5d27e2a7a7822954124d9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/trees/e90de29412689da23c5d27e2a7a7822954124d9c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/commits/16367e8a1eb2489626d593b9bec00adfd2823543","verification":{"payload":"tree e90de29412689da23c5d27e2a7a7822954124d9c\nparent 1fbd94e7301a9c8c82a5f7f2afc735a34884a5d2\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1790235721 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790235721 -0700\n\nDev to Prod (#371)\n\n* chore(deps): update dependency prettier to v3.9.8 (#367)\n\nrenovate updates\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat(components, core): Bubble, Combobox and a shared Diagram, plus column widths\n\nBubble and Combobox are new, for the image agent''s chat and composer. The\nPika diagram renderer moves to components/diagram so other pages can draw\ndiagrams, and gains a Legend. Layout takes a 12-column grid with span on\nits children, Card takes a column count as its size, and columns.scss\ndefines the widths. Scroll reveal, backdrop and the header''s gradient\nshift are now shared utilities.\n\nText resets its padding vars on each element. The sibling spacing used to\ninherit into any Text nested inside, so a legend after a paragraph drew\ntall chips with the value pushed down. The header keeps its last measured\nheight while hidden, and route focus compares paths so StrictMode''s\nsecond run doesn''t focus the page on load.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(portfolio): shared Diagram and tighter copy on the system design page\n\nThe page draws its diagrams with the shared Diagram component. The copy\ndrops pause dashes, colon punchlines and sentences that repeated the one\nbefore, and states each rule before walking through what happens.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(experiments): collapsible sections and plainer copy for the visualiser and tree of life\n\nThe music visualiser''s article sections are Details, like the tree of\nlife''s. Both articles refer to the reader in third person, and lose\nexplanations the reader doesn''t need.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(experiments): Image Agent\n\nA person describes a picture and an agent draws it, asking up to three\nquestions first if the description is too thin. The start page lists\nrunning and past conversations, and has a How it was made article. The\nchat follows one conversation over the ImageAgentThreadUpdated\nsubscription.\n\nOn the experiments home it is No. 3. Its plate is a mosaic of the\nbest-scored pictures, each shown once in the largest grid there are\nenough of them for. Two pictures stack over the whole plate with\nplus-lighter instead of splitting it. Each picture drifts inside its tile\non scroll.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: design system rules for column widths, launch configs and ignore .ua\n\nCLAUDE.md and the Cursor design system rule say widths come from the\n12-column scale. The launch configs cover the backend, the dev server and\na production preview.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(components): Frame, inline link icons, and card and dialog spacing\n\nFrame crops a full-screen view to the window less a gap, with rounded\ncorners. Its top follows the global header, which now publishes how much\nof the window it covers. It eases in from full-bleed by default, and hold\nkeeps a hero in place while it grows into the header''s space. Fixed\nchrome on a framed page clears the frame''s edge.\n\nLink icons flow inline with the text, so a closing arrow follows the\nlast word when it wraps, and the underline follows each line. Cards keep\ntheir padding on small screens, with more room at the foot. Dialogs and\nthe 404/500 pages take their widths from the column scale. The picture\nscrim is a shared mixin.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(image-agent): framed start page, shared backdrop and chat fixes\n\nThe start page is a framed hero with the title, how it works, the field\nand past conversations over the gallery backdrop. With no allowance\nleft, only past conversations show, and the badge stays. In a chat, a\nspent allowance also blocks rewinding and answering. The chat only\nscrolls to the end when the conversation is taller than the window. A\npicture opens full size from anywhere on it, titled after the\nconversation. Chat widths come from the column scale.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(views): frame every full-screen view\n\nThe home page, the experiments stage, the music visualiser and the tree\nof life sit in a Frame. On the stage, each panel''s picture tucks into\nthe frame as it arrives and the words can pass its edge; the Image\nAgent plate uses the shared backdrop, every picture once. The music\nvisualiser and tree of life heroes hold while the frame grows. On the\nhome page the frame eases in before the content. Widths that were\nhand-set now come from the column scale.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(portfolio): column widths for the system design page\n\nThe article body and the fullscreen diagrams use the column scale\ninstead of hand-set widths.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <admin@loci.world>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtNRJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzLIQAKzBjShG5aj8uvMgXn2y47Pb\n7Lkfxrbgeqey6NdN9LbRD1d5Ncn0offrvD7Y39f91YtXM3FU/mORdmPHSyxCLSYK\ngZk9upX3VxSoCl4JfklAs9sKW/jrmCtQZLb6GrglsebSlhgDVs0mIzXTuKCbKlp7\nMtufCTap/z8qGr6en7MwntLjBbgy5yKsUmyOV20KUENB8AhxwPg6fcnaq9+5CUKT\nwuUywX8tIH+9OOA7miVkPdHT+AxWr83l/b00M58nGNwsFT+z/4Y5wsGYbILdxeFU\ns7G/yAPUwZCardgOTwSeEW00VjbLXsBExFqvq/PtnMNrU1CWeXp+O+H59Zehv/6A\n1jrss9idWzc74lcvmOvef1zoGPB/4slYcRJX1ajuKRr8+Vs3IHTfUjKiKnfSrMq+\nmIroQMh+90wmQXz+rvJsNJDxpD+1W3+lhqIaqk7lrKeO2nzIePjkaYQwFmRdOJrh\nFIY/h2KS5tA4tNTL6+cCY6UQnZyEhpciv36vuIMciqXrluCtyPwDnoRXZ5hkIYIG\nFgmOGeHtaJNdbaiKzG8IvTl73QQE0r3PHGKC84zb6eeVkZsn1MpXaHG7SPWzTz1z\nFn3WkWTKGsQs4Ho/YuzqsGnBhDIC1p9Z5Ey/vFhOvQittN5jZde35wMel0ElmYKr\nIDSoCcGJRGVTD+kqKJeC\n=VNxB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T07:42:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kenilam/Ki.CL/commit/16367e8a1eb2489626d593b9bec00adfd2823543","node_id":"C_kwDOAU3gWtoAKDE2MzY3ZThhMWViMjQ4OTYyNmQ1OTNiOWJlYzAwYWRmZDI4MjM1NDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kenilam/Ki.CL/commit/1fbd94e7301a9c8c82a5f7f2afc735a34884a5d2","sha":"1fbd94e7301a9c8c82a5f7f2afc735a34884a5d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/1fbd94e7301a9c8c82a5f7f2afc735a34884a5d2"}],"sha":"16367e8a1eb2489626d593b9bec00adfd2823543","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/16367e8a1eb2489626d593b9bec00adfd2823543"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/1fbd94e7301a9c8c82a5f7f2afc735a34884a5d2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T05:55:37Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T05:55:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Dev to Prod (#370)\n\n* chore(deps): update dependency @types/lodash to v4.17.25 (#350)\n\nrenovate updates\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* ci: open pull requests for new branches and for deployed develop (#363)\n\nA branch gets a pull request to develop on its first push with commits.\nWhen Cloud Build reports the develop deploy as successful, develop gets a\npull request to main, unless one is open or main is already level.\n\nCI now runs on every push instead of on pull requests. Pull requests\nopened by a workflow do not start pull_request runs, so they would never\nshow the build check that develop requires.\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <admin@loci.world>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: move checkout and setup-node to v7 (#365)\n\nv4 of both targets Node 20, which the runners have deprecated and now\nforce onto Node 24 with a warning on every run. v7 targets Node 24.\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <admin@loci.world>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(deps): update commitlint monorepo to v21.2.3 (#366)\n\nrenovate updates\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore(config): migrate config renovate.json (#369)\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat(experiments): bookmark and share actions on the closing screen\n\nThe closing screen gets a short message and an action row with separate\nBookmark and Share parts. Screen padding moves from the panel to the words\nso the plate can reach the edges.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: named exports instead of default exports\n\nEvery module under App now exports by name, so imports use the same name\nthe module declares and renames show up at the import site. React.lazy\ncalls map the named export to `default`, the TreeOfLife version loader\nreads `Canvas`, and route files export their <Route> tree by name.\nvite.config.ts keeps its default export because Vite requires it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: lowercase-dash file and folder names under App\n\nEvery file and folder under App now uses lowercase with dashes\n(Components/HyperLink/Hooks/useURLStatus.tsx becomes\ncomponents/hyper-link/hooks/use-url-status.tsx, Styles.scss becomes\nstyles.scss). Imports, the nested workspace lists, publicDir, the oxlint\nignore path, CLAUDE.md and the Cursor rules follow the new names, and\nyarn.lock picks up the new workspace paths.\n\nJest ignores spec.ts, because its default testMatch would otherwise treat\nthe renamed prop-type files as test suites. README.md keeps its usual name.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(tree-of-life): plate styles load with the plate, and dead version files go\n\nTaxonVisual used the v14 class root, and its plate rules lived in the v14\nstylesheet. v15 shows the plate without loading that file, so the plate\nlost its square shape and rounded corners unless v14 had been opened\nfirst. It now has its own folder, class root and styles.scss.\n\nv9 to v12 only re-export v13, so their layout engines and stylesheets were\nnever loaded. versions/styles.scss was an old copy of the selector styles\nthat nothing imported, and v15''s __stage rule matched no element.\n\nShare imported the closing screen''s stylesheet without using any of it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(widgets, router): split global header and status pages into parts\n\nThe global header''s contents and its block-size style tag are now their\nown files, and the mobile navigation''s open and close toggles are parts\nof their own, the close toggle taking its overlay styles with it.\n\nThe 204 and 500 pages shared the same go-back link, so it is one part\nboth render. The 404 page''s go-back link and message are parts too.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(components): split details, dialog, list, radio group, input group and popover into parts\n\nEach inner part is its own file, or a folder when it has styles, and reads\nwhat it needs from a context at the component root instead of props. The\npublic exports and props are unchanged. The dialog close button now gets\nits position from utility classes instead of SCSS.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(components): split select, calendar and date picker into parts\n\nSelect, Calendar and DatePicker each get a root context, and their trigger,\ncontent, item, header, grid and day parts move into folders with their own\nstyles. Pure date helpers move to helpers.ts. The public exports and props\nare unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(views): split the views root, experiments home screen and more into parts\n\nThe views root keeps only the router tree; the header show/hide contents\nand the body effect are their own files. Each experiments home screen gets\na context, and its words and plate move into folders with their styles and\nkeyframes. The closing screen''s action row and the home header aside''s\npadding get their own files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(tree-of-life): split v15, the version selector and home into parts\n\nv15''s index only composes: scene, controls and panel are their own files.\nDepth and CameraRig read focus from the context and take no props. Labels\nbecome a folder with a store, grid helpers, a placement loop, the projector\nand their styles. Search and the version selector''s toggle get folders\nwith their styles, Growing moves out of the taxon guard, and the home\nbanner intro and each article section are their own files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(music-visualiser): track context and smaller parts\n\nA track context at the track root replaces the props Chrome, Controls,\nNowPlaying and Gate were given. Copy link and volume are their own parts,\nand the chrome''s styles move to the parts that use them. The home article\nsections, the banner words and the chevron are their own files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(portfolio): split sign-in and the system design page into parts\n\nSign-in''s header, fields and error are their own files, reading the form\nthrough useFormContext. The system design page''s scroll indicator, hero,\ndiagrams, build plan, simulation player and anchor nav move into folders\nwith their styles, the player and nav get contexts, and each part-one and\npart-two subsection is its own file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(env): anchor the /env dev proxy to the exact path\n\nVite matches plain proxy keys as prefixes, so /env also caught source\nfiles under App/env/* and answered them with JSON. The browser then\nrefused /env/client/index.tsx as a module and the app failed to load.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(tree-of-life): load the context with the route chunk\n\nTreeOfLifeProvider was imported statically by the route file, and the\nversions selector (which reads the context) was too, so the context and\nits API hooks shipped before anyone opened Tree of Life. The provider now\nlives in the lazy contents, the session gate moves to session.tsx, and the\nversions layout loads through the route''s lazy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(server): import Env by name\n\ne930dece switched App/env to a named export but left the server on a\ndefault import, so the container exited at startup with \"does not provide\nan export named ''default''\" and Cloud Run never saw the port open.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: semantic markup, CSS over JS and existing classes in CLAUDE.md\n\nThese are the standards for new work: choose the element that means the\nthing and keep markup valid, prefer CSS to JS where CSS can do the job, and\nuse existing utility classes before adding SCSS.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(client): match lowercase folders when assigning style layers\n\nThe lowercase rename left getStyleLayer checking Core/Styles/, Views/ and\nRouter/, so every stylesheet fell into the components layer. In the built\nsite .kicl-layout then beat .kicl--icons--logo again and shrank the logo to\nits padding. The Cursor alias rule example also still named Components.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(a11y): site-wide semantics, skip link, focus and page width\n\nNavigation now renders nav > ul > li; it put li straight into nav, which is\ninvalid in every header. index.html closes app-root properly, stops\nblocking pinch zoom, puts charset first and drops stale meta.\n\nA skip link leads to main, and a route change moves focus to main the way\na page load would. The focus outline shows on keyboard focus only, at 2px\nwith an offset. Anchors stop below the fixed header.\n\nThe logo is a named link, not an h1 on every page. The home page''s h1 is\nits logo. The duplicate banner roles are gone, the mobile navigation\ndialog has a name, and decorative icons are hidden from screen readers.\n\nBody, view and header widths no longer use 100vw, which counted the\nscrollbar and scrolled the page sideways. The error page says Ki.CL, sits\nin main and shows the stack as code.\n\nText can now render code, em, pre, strong and time. CLAUDE.md asks for\ntypes inferred from elements and components instead of inline shapes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: disabled buttons, switch animation, phases table and v15 search\n\nButton''s disabled colours targeted `.disabled`, a class the component\nnever emits; they now match its disabled modifier, `:disabled` and\naria-disabled. The unused cursor variable is gone.\n\nThe switch thumb moves with `translate` but the transition named\n`transform`, so it never animated.\n\nLayout''s full-screen rule read a variable that was never defined; the\nline did nothing and is removed.\n\nThe phases table gave header and body cells different padding, so the\ncolumns did not line up. Both now use the same padding classes.\n\nThe v15 search input was disabled during each search, which dropped\nfocus and keystrokes while typing. Labels now avoid the side panel and\ncontrols; their selector matched nothing before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(styles): z-index scale, full gutter classes, header offset and block sizes\n\nz-index values were hand-picked numbers from 0 to 100002. They now come\nfrom one scale named by role (raised, floating, popover, overlay, header,\ntop), keeping the order they had.\n\nThe gutter classes stopped at widest and skipped the base size; they now\ninclude both, plus kicl-margin-inline-auto. New classes clear the fixed\nheader (kicl-padding-block-start-header, kicl-inset-block-start-header)\nand set block sizes (kicl-block-size-full, -screen, kicl-min-block-size-screen).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(styles): clear the Sass if() deprecation warnings\n\nThe build printed about 550 deprecation warnings. Our two if() calls are\nnow @if blocks. The rest came from include-media 2.0.0, the latest\nrelease, so quietDeps hides warnings from dependencies while ours still\nshow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(components): native form controls\n\nRadio group, checkbox, switch and select are native inputs now, so the\nbrowser supplies keyboard handling, form values and labels, and the state\nthat mirrored the DOM is gone. Select opts into appearance: base-select\nand falls back to a plain native select; its positioning hook and\noutside-click listener are removed.\n\nCalendar is a table named by its month, with full-date labels on each day.\nDatePicker forwards the id and aria props FormControl gives it. Form\npasses required to its controls, merges aria-describedby, and only\nannounces real errors. Input group addons follow DOM order, and invalid\nborders now turn red on themed pages.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(components): semantic content components and native hash links\n\nImage drops the empty object wrapper and requires alt. AnimatedText is\nread as one string. Spinner and Status announce themselves, Skeleton is\nhidden from screen readers and stops pulsing under reduced motion, and\nSeparator is an hr when it carries meaning. Heading takes lookLike, Dialog\ntakes a title, and Popover content is named by its trigger.\n\nSame-page hash links are plain anchors, so the browser scrolls and moves\nfocus itself. That removes the skip link''s focus handler, the music\nvisualiser''s offset span and the unused scroll-into-view hook. Duplicate\nfocus and cursor rules, which the global styles already set, are gone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(experiments): semantic markup and utility classes for experiments home and the music visualiser\n\nExperiments home gets a hidden h1, with each screen title as h2, and every\n''See the experience'' link names its experiment. Share now shares, or\ncopies the link where the Web Share API is missing. The closing screen is\na labelled section, and route shells are divs rather than headingless\nsections.\n\nThe music visualiser player has an h1, copy link is a button, only the\ntitle is announced on track change, and the gate names the track it\nplays. The full-bleed width hacks give way to utility classes for width,\nblock size, padding and the header offset.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(tree-of-life): semantic markup, native details and utility classes\n\nThe essay''s parts are labelled sections, the nested article is a div, and\n''Fifteen attempts'' is a real heading over lists of eras. v15 has a hidden\nh1, one labelled aside with a search landmark and a details section, a\nnamed canvas and a labelled nav of taxa. Toggles are named by their\nvisible text. Details state comes from the native element rather than a\ncopy in React, and the banner switches layout with a media query instead\nof useResponsive. The taxon plate is a figure whose result is announced.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(portfolio): heading order, real links and semantic content for the system design page\n\nThe hero is the page h1, sections are h2 and subsections h3, with ids set\nin JSX instead of matched at runtime. The anchor nav uses links to those\nids. Diagrams are figures holding their open button, with the\ndescription as caption. Prompts and the simulation log are ordered\nlists, lead-ins are strong, dates are time elements, and the phases\ntable has a caption and row headers. The run button stays focusable while\na run plays. Sign-in has an h1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(home, widgets, router): status headings, CSS header gap and simpler infinite scroll\n\nStatus pages lead with the status as h1, the 404 path is code, and one\ngo-back link remains. The global header''s gap comes from a media query\ninstead of useResponsive. InfiniteScroll sets its speed inline and stays\nin flow, so the per-render style tag and ResizeObserver are gone. Company\nicons are named by the company. The home page drops 100dvw and uses\nutility classes, and its contact links are a labelled nav.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: regressions found in the end-to-end run\n\nFound by comparing the site in Chrome with a build from before the audit.\n\n- The Vite proxy sent any path starting /assets/taxon-visual to the\n  backend, which included the site''s own taxon-visual chunk after the\n  rename, so v15 failed to load. The rule now needs the trailing slash.\n- External links gained hidden \"(opens in a new tab)\" text, which broke\n  the icon-only button style, so the home contact icons lost their\n  circles. The rule now ignores visually hidden text and skips unstyled\n  buttons.\n- The experiments shell centred a content-sized track, so full-width\n  pages shrank to their content once the 100dvi workaround went. The\n  track now stretches.\n- The era labels under Fifteen attempts go back below their numbers,\n  still naming each list; the 404 path stays bold; the header nav is\n  labelled Main.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <admin@loci.world>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"039156b7db52fc6383af30b8868efcbb538969c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/trees/039156b7db52fc6383af30b8868efcbb538969c3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/commits/1fbd94e7301a9c8c82a5f7f2afc735a34884a5d2","verification":{"payload":"tree 039156b7db52fc6383af30b8868efcbb538969c3\nparent 04c36f8ddc32b9764fe72f13b5c99861894c5ee4\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1790056537 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790056537 -0700\n\nDev to Prod (#370)\n\n* chore(deps): update dependency @types/lodash to v4.17.25 (#350)\n\nrenovate updates\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* ci: open pull requests for new branches and for deployed develop (#363)\n\nA branch gets a pull request to develop on its first push with commits.\nWhen Cloud Build reports the develop deploy as successful, develop gets a\npull request to main, unless one is open or main is already level.\n\nCI now runs on every push instead of on pull requests. Pull requests\nopened by a workflow do not start pull_request runs, so they would never\nshow the build check that develop requires.\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <admin@loci.world>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: move checkout and setup-node to v7 (#365)\n\nv4 of both targets Node 20, which the runners have deprecated and now\nforce onto Node 24 with a warning on every run. v7 targets Node 24.\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <admin@loci.world>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(deps): update commitlint monorepo to v21.2.3 (#366)\n\nrenovate updates\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore(config): migrate config renovate.json (#369)\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat(experiments): bookmark and share actions on the closing screen\n\nThe closing screen gets a short message and an action row with separate\nBookmark and Share parts. Screen padding moves from the panel to the words\nso the plate can reach the edges.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: named exports instead of default exports\n\nEvery module under App now exports by name, so imports use the same name\nthe module declares and renames show up at the import site. React.lazy\ncalls map the named export to `default`, the TreeOfLife version loader\nreads `Canvas`, and route files export their <Route> tree by name.\nvite.config.ts keeps its default export because Vite requires it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: lowercase-dash file and folder names under App\n\nEvery file and folder under App now uses lowercase with dashes\n(Components/HyperLink/Hooks/useURLStatus.tsx becomes\ncomponents/hyper-link/hooks/use-url-status.tsx, Styles.scss becomes\nstyles.scss). Imports, the nested workspace lists, publicDir, the oxlint\nignore path, CLAUDE.md and the Cursor rules follow the new names, and\nyarn.lock picks up the new workspace paths.\n\nJest ignores spec.ts, because its default testMatch would otherwise treat\nthe renamed prop-type files as test suites. README.md keeps its usual name.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(tree-of-life): plate styles load with the plate, and dead version files go\n\nTaxonVisual used the v14 class root, and its plate rules lived in the v14\nstylesheet. v15 shows the plate without loading that file, so the plate\nlost its square shape and rounded corners unless v14 had been opened\nfirst. It now has its own folder, class root and styles.scss.\n\nv9 to v12 only re-export v13, so their layout engines and stylesheets were\nnever loaded. versions/styles.scss was an old copy of the selector styles\nthat nothing imported, and v15''s __stage rule matched no element.\n\nShare imported the closing screen''s stylesheet without using any of it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(widgets, router): split global header and status pages into parts\n\nThe global header''s contents and its block-size style tag are now their\nown files, and the mobile navigation''s open and close toggles are parts\nof their own, the close toggle taking its overlay styles with it.\n\nThe 204 and 500 pages shared the same go-back link, so it is one part\nboth render. The 404 page''s go-back link and message are parts too.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(components): split details, dialog, list, radio group, input group and popover into parts\n\nEach inner part is its own file, or a folder when it has styles, and reads\nwhat it needs from a context at the component root instead of props. The\npublic exports and props are unchanged. The dialog close button now gets\nits position from utility classes instead of SCSS.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(components): split select, calendar and date picker into parts\n\nSelect, Calendar and DatePicker each get a root context, and their trigger,\ncontent, item, header, grid and day parts move into folders with their own\nstyles. Pure date helpers move to helpers.ts. The public exports and props\nare unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(views): split the views root, experiments home screen and more into parts\n\nThe views root keeps only the router tree; the header show/hide contents\nand the body effect are their own files. Each experiments home screen gets\na context, and its words and plate move into folders with their styles and\nkeyframes. The closing screen''s action row and the home header aside''s\npadding get their own files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(tree-of-life): split v15, the version selector and home into parts\n\nv15''s index only composes: scene, controls and panel are their own files.\nDepth and CameraRig read focus from the context and take no props. Labels\nbecome a folder with a store, grid helpers, a placement loop, the projector\nand their styles. Search and the version selector''s toggle get folders\nwith their styles, Growing moves out of the taxon guard, and the home\nbanner intro and each article section are their own files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(music-visualiser): track context and smaller parts\n\nA track context at the track root replaces the props Chrome, Controls,\nNowPlaying and Gate were given. Copy link and volume are their own parts,\nand the chrome''s styles move to the parts that use them. The home article\nsections, the banner words and the chevron are their own files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(portfolio): split sign-in and the system design page into parts\n\nSign-in''s header, fields and error are their own files, reading the form\nthrough useFormContext. The system design page''s scroll indicator, hero,\ndiagrams, build plan, simulation player and anchor nav move into folders\nwith their styles, the player and nav get contexts, and each part-one and\npart-two subsection is its own file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(env): anchor the /env dev proxy to the exact path\n\nVite matches plain proxy keys as prefixes, so /env also caught source\nfiles under App/env/* and answered them with JSON. The browser then\nrefused /env/client/index.tsx as a module and the app failed to load.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(tree-of-life): load the context with the route chunk\n\nTreeOfLifeProvider was imported statically by the route file, and the\nversions selector (which reads the context) was too, so the context and\nits API hooks shipped before anyone opened Tree of Life. The provider now\nlives in the lazy contents, the session gate moves to session.tsx, and the\nversions layout loads through the route''s lazy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(server): import Env by name\n\ne930dece switched App/env to a named export but left the server on a\ndefault import, so the container exited at startup with \"does not provide\nan export named ''default''\" and Cloud Run never saw the port open.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: semantic markup, CSS over JS and existing classes in CLAUDE.md\n\nThese are the standards for new work: choose the element that means the\nthing and keep markup valid, prefer CSS to JS where CSS can do the job, and\nuse existing utility classes before adding SCSS.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(client): match lowercase folders when assigning style layers\n\nThe lowercase rename left getStyleLayer checking Core/Styles/, Views/ and\nRouter/, so every stylesheet fell into the components layer. In the built\nsite .kicl-layout then beat .kicl--icons--logo again and shrank the logo to\nits padding. The Cursor alias rule example also still named Components.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(a11y): site-wide semantics, skip link, focus and page width\n\nNavigation now renders nav > ul > li; it put li straight into nav, which is\ninvalid in every header. index.html closes app-root properly, stops\nblocking pinch zoom, puts charset first and drops stale meta.\n\nA skip link leads to main, and a route change moves focus to main the way\na page load would. The focus outline shows on keyboard focus only, at 2px\nwith an offset. Anchors stop below the fixed header.\n\nThe logo is a named link, not an h1 on every page. The home page''s h1 is\nits logo. The duplicate banner roles are gone, the mobile navigation\ndialog has a name, and decorative icons are hidden from screen readers.\n\nBody, view and header widths no longer use 100vw, which counted the\nscrollbar and scrolled the page sideways. The error page says Ki.CL, sits\nin main and shows the stack as code.\n\nText can now render code, em, pre, strong and time. CLAUDE.md asks for\ntypes inferred from elements and components instead of inline shapes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: disabled buttons, switch animation, phases table and v15 search\n\nButton''s disabled colours targeted `.disabled`, a class the component\nnever emits; they now match its disabled modifier, `:disabled` and\naria-disabled. The unused cursor variable is gone.\n\nThe switch thumb moves with `translate` but the transition named\n`transform`, so it never animated.\n\nLayout''s full-screen rule read a variable that was never defined; the\nline did nothing and is removed.\n\nThe phases table gave header and body cells different padding, so the\ncolumns did not line up. Both now use the same padding classes.\n\nThe v15 search input was disabled during each search, which dropped\nfocus and keystrokes while typing. Labels now avoid the side panel and\ncontrols; their selector matched nothing before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(styles): z-index scale, full gutter classes, header offset and block sizes\n\nz-index values were hand-picked numbers from 0 to 100002. They now come\nfrom one scale named by role (raised, floating, popover, overlay, header,\ntop), keeping the order they had.\n\nThe gutter classes stopped at widest and skipped the base size; they now\ninclude both, plus kicl-margin-inline-auto. New classes clear the fixed\nheader (kicl-padding-block-start-header, kicl-inset-block-start-header)\nand set block sizes (kicl-block-size-full, -screen, kicl-min-block-size-screen).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(styles): clear the Sass if() deprecation warnings\n\nThe build printed about 550 deprecation warnings. Our two if() calls are\nnow @if blocks. The rest came from include-media 2.0.0, the latest\nrelease, so quietDeps hides warnings from dependencies while ours still\nshow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(components): native form controls\n\nRadio group, checkbox, switch and select are native inputs now, so the\nbrowser supplies keyboard handling, form values and labels, and the state\nthat mirrored the DOM is gone. Select opts into appearance: base-select\nand falls back to a plain native select; its positioning hook and\noutside-click listener are removed.\n\nCalendar is a table named by its month, with full-date labels on each day.\nDatePicker forwards the id and aria props FormControl gives it. Form\npasses required to its controls, merges aria-describedby, and only\nannounces real errors. Input group addons follow DOM order, and invalid\nborders now turn red on themed pages.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(components): semantic content components and native hash links\n\nImage drops the empty object wrapper and requires alt. AnimatedText is\nread as one string. Spinner and Status announce themselves, Skeleton is\nhidden from screen readers and stops pulsing under reduced motion, and\nSeparator is an hr when it carries meaning. Heading takes lookLike, Dialog\ntakes a title, and Popover content is named by its trigger.\n\nSame-page hash links are plain anchors, so the browser scrolls and moves\nfocus itself. That removes the skip link''s focus handler, the music\nvisualiser''s offset span and the unused scroll-into-view hook. Duplicate\nfocus and cursor rules, which the global styles already set, are gone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(experiments): semantic markup and utility classes for experiments home and the music visualiser\n\nExperiments home gets a hidden h1, with each screen title as h2, and every\n''See the experience'' link names its experiment. Share now shares, or\ncopies the link where the Web Share API is missing. The closing screen is\na labelled section, and route shells are divs rather than headingless\nsections.\n\nThe music visualiser player has an h1, copy link is a button, only the\ntitle is announced on track change, and the gate names the track it\nplays. The full-bleed width hacks give way to utility classes for width,\nblock size, padding and the header offset.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(tree-of-life): semantic markup, native details and utility classes\n\nThe essay''s parts are labelled sections, the nested article is a div, and\n''Fifteen attempts'' is a real heading over lists of eras. v15 has a hidden\nh1, one labelled aside with a search landmark and a details section, a\nnamed canvas and a labelled nav of taxa. Toggles are named by their\nvisible text. Details state comes from the native element rather than a\ncopy in React, and the banner switches layout with a media query instead\nof useResponsive. The taxon plate is a figure whose result is announced.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(portfolio): heading order, real links and semantic content for the system design page\n\nThe hero is the page h1, sections are h2 and subsections h3, with ids set\nin JSX instead of matched at runtime. The anchor nav uses links to those\nids. Diagrams are figures holding their open button, with the\ndescription as caption. Prompts and the simulation log are ordered\nlists, lead-ins are strong, dates are time elements, and the phases\ntable has a caption and row headers. The run button stays focusable while\na run plays. Sign-in has an h1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(home, widgets, router): status headings, CSS header gap and simpler infinite scroll\n\nStatus pages lead with the status as h1, the 404 path is code, and one\ngo-back link remains. The global header''s gap comes from a media query\ninstead of useResponsive. InfiniteScroll sets its speed inline and stays\nin flow, so the per-render style tag and ResizeObserver are gone. Company\nicons are named by the company. The home page drops 100dvw and uses\nutility classes, and its contact links are a labelled nav.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: regressions found in the end-to-end run\n\nFound by comparing the site in Chrome with a build from before the audit.\n\n- The Vite proxy sent any path starting /assets/taxon-visual to the\n  backend, which included the site''s own taxon-visual chunk after the\n  rename, so v15 failed to load. The rule now needs the trailing slash.\n- External links gained hidden \"(opens in a new tab)\" text, which broke\n  the icon-only button style, so the home contact icons lost their\n  circles. The rule now ignores visually hidden text and skips unstyled\n  buttons.\n- The experiments shell centred a content-sized track, so full-width\n  pages shrank to their content once the 100dvi workaround went. The\n  track now stretches.\n- The era labels under Fifteen attempts go back below their numbers,\n  still naming each list; the 404 path stays bold; the header nav is\n  labelled Main.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <admin@loci.world>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqshhZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArJ0QAIbkBrDiJZj/lqEcatA5OWvs\n6BuvKkCr9/kP3ulMZinpnms+xs9+uqTuNa0+spac0dXexWibMFw75qswgqTRfpJa\n49n8xXeyCI/34yFVFp/9PBGdEgKFV4xfIQHKg08XQBukPHKOTXy+CtWktMHwHWsj\nODpyTuMp1f2zGumGiVTQ+SH0hxxOzb7m4BsGLaVtekw1ZcldC2+bu/U0tlUjaqvp\nF2qTyrpQ6qSazxcvksEPZH1jdznkYmwsLDh1KmPf+no16eeFDfOU7ykrRLWlZqRd\n/V9Ci5lC+C7iEp+tcwyy+qoMriW79tf8e044VcqFO2is/ji/Ken2BIF0ANnVT7Wg\nkfsrPv1BdDkAgjNrASdr9ydJ/ID3afGKnhWEMXBDlyHiFRm2tRi+snURjPcqQmKt\nWX4ucSsZAc6ieK/WISwUnXVgSMt2PfXKV9jTJWbaqc6N2mDYXXzgO9uCO2Rtlxgv\n5DQTmvTpoK3c8adhmMXrVqIZ0r2ka74rcb77UU7q7FPZl7hoZjr3+n2uWkbjFZR7\nP5GqMa5O7n9b33HCgcEv+A0+xCTp2UfAX0yuctQxWuEBF28cYZBQjTiCAsKODCgf\nBoePW+HrO5smTOBTVGuzn8h89Mc7kBhlVH5UkemeilTaSQoKOvMoMhC20VdxfC/g\nj6aRF0K0pNPF4N+fS1ba\n=HnBX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T05:55:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kenilam/Ki.CL/commit/1fbd94e7301a9c8c82a5f7f2afc735a34884a5d2","node_id":"C_kwDOAU3gWtoAKDFmYmQ5NGU3MzAxYTljOGM4MmE1ZjdmMmFmYzczNWEzNDg4NGE1ZDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kenilam/Ki.CL/commit/04c36f8ddc32b9764fe72f13b5c99861894c5ee4","sha":"04c36f8ddc32b9764fe72f13b5c99861894c5ee4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/04c36f8ddc32b9764fe72f13b5c99861894c5ee4"}],"sha":"1fbd94e7301a9c8c82a5f7f2afc735a34884a5d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/1fbd94e7301a9c8c82a5f7f2afc735a34884a5d2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/657845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kenilam","id":657845,"login":"kenilam","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1Nzg0NQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/04c36f8ddc32b9764fe72f13b5c99861894c5ee4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T23:29:47Z","email":"657845+kenilam@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Keni"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T23:29:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Dev to Prod (#364)\n\n* chore(deps): update dependency @types/lodash to v4.17.25 (#350)\n\nrenovate updates\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* ci: open pull requests for new branches and for deployed develop (#363)\n\nA branch gets a pull request to develop on its first push with commits.\nWhen Cloud Build reports the develop deploy as successful, develop gets a\npull request to main, unless one is open or main is already level.\n\nCI now runs on every push instead of on pull requests. Pull requests\nopened by a workflow do not start pull_request runs, so they would never\nshow the build check that develop requires.\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <admin@loci.world>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: move checkout and setup-node to v7 (#365)\n\nv4 of both targets Node 20, which the runners have deprecated and now\nforce onto Node 24 with a warning on every run. v7 targets Node 24.\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <admin@loci.world>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <admin@loci.world>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cf533bdb4bff04975fe3b8ae0eaf76d239149166","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/trees/cf533bdb4bff04975fe3b8ae0eaf76d239149166"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/commits/04c36f8ddc32b9764fe72f13b5c99861894c5ee4","verification":{"payload":"tree cf533bdb4bff04975fe3b8ae0eaf76d239149166\nparent f43550b958f19e7fbc81df1e56b4e2edcad3f5d5\nauthor Keni <657845+kenilam@users.noreply.github.com> 1790033387 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790033387 -0700\n\nDev to Prod (#364)\n\n* chore(deps): update dependency @types/lodash to v4.17.25 (#350)\n\nrenovate updates\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* ci: open pull requests for new branches and for deployed develop (#363)\n\nA branch gets a pull request to develop on its first push with commits.\nWhen Cloud Build reports the develop deploy as successful, develop gets a\npull request to main, unless one is open or main is already level.\n\nCI now runs on every push instead of on pull requests. Pull requests\nopened by a workflow do not start pull_request runs, so they would never\nshow the build check that develop requires.\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <admin@loci.world>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: move checkout and setup-node to v7 (#365)\n\nv4 of both targets Node 20, which the runners have deprecated and now\nforce onto Node 24 with a warning on every run. v7 targets Node 24.\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <admin@loci.world>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <admin@loci.world>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsb3rCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyvIQABzCgiLKaG/saEMbHeANrJLK\nDV+S0AISSlUcFIAKv2Vp2sMAkQ1ga8U9tP/EYlwPIIPkWMhrUZmrXXqSSZ5fO/8H\n473y8RJ5lR0dm3+KWL6KDTZk42ALS0I52YR/+BkFawGoXRd9XvdTZtiS/QUNqdSi\nmOW0obFo0a0/ABY5352oG+dtgJWRercdADiJs662P1dVj2Y25t9TfdN42G5BGJsE\nWkmBFOVJWdJLQZdo19SoIP3EI59cEDdmxArdJL7lVCbJzPorgqRNaeB67Pfu6r5N\nfI4nSY4DO32Pw9dkJ6poC6vaUF6TwxA8VsMJCWRpdrevNx1V2SAaQ7rTzi3+z3nZ\nqeAbx8NVXyH90CP1QWGdCi39DVaFSLO0XjBcx9w2wac/YCIKC3wldqeNRut/C25g\n8WgS