DNkMTFlMGQ0NGI5OTA1Nzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kenilam/Ki.CL/commit/d8c17343bfcddca0f25148359984de4a822395ea","sha":"d8c17343bfcddca0f25148359984de4a822395ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/d8c17343bfcddca0f25148359984de4a822395ea"}],"sha":"afc195981642e531e394843d3d11e0d44b990577","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/afc195981642e531e394843d3d11e0d44b990577"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/d8c17343bfcddca0f25148359984de4a822395ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T04:33:12Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T04:33:12Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"docs(experiments): scope the music visualiser\n\nA note in the folder the experiment will live in, carrying the research\nand decisions from the session that scoped it: where the music can come\nfrom and why, the proxy-and-adapter design, and what it takes to run the\napp in a cloud session.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015PtptZTnD2MMdMd4awfU73","tree":{"sha":"4018b4dc5448f31fd9e65d64a1abbfccf7f80757","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/trees/4018b4dc5448f31fd9e65d64a1abbfccf7f80757"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/commits/d8c17343bfcddca0f25148359984de4a822395ea","verification":{"payload":"tree 4018b4dc5448f31fd9e65d64a1abbfccf7f80757\nparent bc03948b9abf093e80970eca0762627e0f610c26\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789878792 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789878792 +0000\n\ndocs(experiments): scope the music visualiser\n\nA note in the folder the experiment will live in, carrying the research\nand decisions from the session that scoped it: where the music can come\nfrom and why, the proxy-and-adapter design, and what it takes to run the\napp in a cloud session.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015PtptZTnD2MMdMd4awfU73\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHnoVgT2\nE18yb9nQl0vSPKNLkeYCigQROFIpw5WDP5dVPsdeqELLgSwLmGkOa94ihddrqAQTyJR3nLqPx36q\nPwA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T04:33:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kenilam/Ki.CL/commit/d8c17343bfcddca0f25148359984de4a822395ea","node_id":"C_kwDOAU3gWtoAKGQ4YzE3MzQzYmZjZGRjYTBmMjUxNDgzNTk5ODRkZTRhODIyMzk1ZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kenilam/Ki.CL/commit/bc03948b9abf093e80970eca0762627e0f610c26","sha":"bc03948b9abf093e80970eca0762627e0f610c26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/bc03948b9abf093e80970eca0762627e0f610c26"}],"sha":"d8c17343bfcddca0f25148359984de4a822395ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/d8c17343bfcddca0f25148359984de4a822395ea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/657845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kenilam","id":657845,"login":"kenilam","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1Nzg0NQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/commits/bc03948b9abf093e80970eca0762627e0f610c26/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T04:12:35Z","email":"657845+kenilam@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Keni"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T04:12:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Replace gradient background with GPU-rendered dithered light (#358)\n\n* feat(home): replace the gradient with a dithered light\n\nThe home page backed its copy with a five-colour linear gradient, animated\nby sliding its background position over five minutes. Softened to pastels\nso the text stayed readable, it read as a washed-out rainbow.\n\nIt is now an ordered-dither render: three solid brand inks laid down as\noverlapping pools of light on plain paper, mixed only by a Bayer 8x8\nthreshold at four pixels a cell, the way early print faked tone. Nothing is\never blended, so the colours stay at full strength, and the grain is the\ntexture. A soft clearing in the middle keeps the copy on bare paper at any\nviewport.\n\nThe renderer is a canvas behind the header, drawn at one pixel per cell\nand scaled up with `image-rendering: pixelated`. The pools drift on their\nown slow cycles at ten frames a second; anyone asking for reduced motion\ngets a single still frame. Every colour and the cell size are custom\nproperties on the canvas, so the theme owns the palette - the dark theme\nswaps paper and inks without a script change - and the canvas re-reads\nthem when the theme class on `body` changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015PtptZTnD2MMdMd4awfU73\n\n* feat(home): render the background as a dithered gradient, not a posterised one\n\nThe first pass dithered three flat inks at four-pixel blocks, which read as\npixel art. The reference is the print sense of the term: colour that blends\ncontinuously, with a fine ordered screen laid over it as texture.\n\nThe renderer is now a fragment shader. Four soft pools of ink are mixed in\nOklab over the paper, with a small chroma push where they meet so the\ntransitions stay vivid, then each pixel is quantised to fourteen tones\nagainst a Bayer 8x8 threshold at two-pixel cells, with a whisper of grain.\nThe clearing behind the copy keeps a little colour rather than draining to\npaper. Palettes are derived from the brand blue, orange, red, yellow and\nwhite in the stylesheet: a print on cream in light, a deep field with an\nelectric glow, warm rim and cream band in dark.\n\nRendering at device resolution needs the GPU; where WebGL is unavailable\nthe page shows its paper. A lost context is set up again on restore.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015PtptZTnD2MMdMd4awfU73\n\n* fix(home): keep the dark field inside the HSL gamut\n\nSass emitted the deep blue with 103% saturation, which browsers clamp but\nwhich is not a value to ship. A smaller push lands just under 100%.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015PtptZTnD2MMdMd4awfU73\n\n* style(home): sink the background inks into the theme\n\nEvery ink is now mixed most of the way into its theme''s paper in the\nstylesheet, and the chroma push after the mix is gone. The light is meant\nto sit inside the page rather than on top of it: a tint that reads as\natmosphere, not as colour.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015PtptZTnD2MMdMd4awfU73\n\n* style(home): a visible drift, a darker dark, a finer screen\n\nThe pools now travel a tenth of the viewport on cycles of fifteen to twenty\nseconds; at the previous amplitude the motion was below what anyone would\nnotice. The dark inks sink further into the black, so the page stays a dark\npage with light in it. And the screen is now one device-scaled pixel at\nforty-eight tones: the dither becomes a fine grain rather than a weave.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015PtptZTnD2MMdMd4awfU73\n\n* style(home): sink dark further, quicken the drift\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015PtptZTnD2MMdMd4awfU73\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"adc48aee079a1590c8a27ba5a755c433231a07f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/trees/adc48aee079a1590c8a27ba5a755c433231a07f3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL/git/commits/bc03948b9abf093e80970eca0762627e0f610c26","verification":{"payload":"tree adc48aee079a1590c8a27ba5a755c433231a07f3\nparent 1452b80f4918b3d86b2474b6a74e09a9e54bdde4\nauthor Keni <657845+kenilam@users.noreply.github.com> 1789877555 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789877555 -0700\n\nReplace gradient background with GPU-rendered dithered light (#358)\n\n* feat(home): replace the gradient with a dithered light\n\nThe home page backed its copy with a five-colour linear gradient, animated\nby sliding its background position over five minutes. Softened to pastels\nso the text stayed readable, it read as a washed-out rainbow.\n\nIt is now an ordered-dither render: three solid brand inks laid down as\noverlapping pools of light on plain paper, mixed only by a Bayer 8x8\nthreshold at four pixels a cell, the way early print faked tone. Nothing is\never blended, so the colours stay at full strength, and the grain is the\ntexture. A soft clearing in the middle keeps the copy on bare paper at any\nviewport.\n\nThe renderer is a canvas behind the header, drawn at one pixel per cell\nand scaled up with `image-rendering: pixelated`. The pools drift on their\nown slow cycles at ten frames a second; anyone asking for reduced motion\ngets a single still frame. Every colour and the cell size are custom\nproperties on the canvas, so the theme owns the palette - the dark theme\nswaps paper and inks without a script change - and the canvas re-reads\nthem when the theme class on `body` changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015PtptZTnD2MMdMd4awfU73\n\n* feat(home): render the background as a dithered gradient, not a posterised one\n\nThe first pass dithered three flat inks at four-pixel blocks, which read as\npixel art. The reference is the print sense of the term: colour that blends\ncontinuously, with a fine ordered screen laid over it as texture.\n\nThe renderer is now a fragment shader. Four soft pools of ink are mixed in\nOklab over the paper, with a small chroma push where they meet so the\ntransitions stay vivid, then each pixel is quantised to fourteen tones\nagainst a Bayer 8x8 threshold at two-pixel cells, with a whisper of grain.\nThe clearing behind the copy keeps a little colour rather than draining to\npaper. Palettes are derived from the brand blue, orange, red, yellow and\nwhite in the stylesheet: a print on cream in light, a deep field with an\nelectric glow, warm rim and cream band in dark.\n\nRendering at device resolution needs the GPU; where WebGL is unavailable\nthe page shows its paper. A lost context is set up again on restore.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015PtptZTnD2MMdMd4awfU73\n\n* fix(home): keep the dark field inside the HSL gamut\n\nSass emitted the deep blue with 103% saturation, which browsers clamp but\nwhich is not a value to ship. A smaller push lands just under 100%.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015PtptZTnD2MMdMd4awfU73\n\n* style(home): sink the background inks into the theme\n\nEvery ink is now mixed most of the way into its theme''s paper in the\nstylesheet, and the chroma push after the mix is gone. The light is meant\nto sit inside the page rather than on top of it: a tint that reads as\natmosphere, not as colour.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015PtptZTnD2MMdMd4awfU73\n\n* style(home): a visible drift, a darker dark, a finer screen\n\nThe pools now travel a tenth of the viewport on cycles of fifteen to twenty\nseconds; at the previous amplitude the motion was below what anyone would\nnotice. The dark inks sink further into the black, so the page stays a dark\npage with light in it. And the screen is now one device-scaled pixel at\nforty-eight tones: the dither becomes a fine grain rather than a weave.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015PtptZTnD2MMdMd4awfU73\n\n* style(home): sink dark further, quicken the drift\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015PtptZTnD2MMdMd4awfU73\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqr10zCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACxgQAIOsOxIOyGtLdlJMLOZWli31\n7cZyOBTPq8jpefi8YMsvANNJdx7qTvWfD2uxdhqrsBugclOToPaHdejeoa3bAfVU\niT8xxumDYudLHv2lx1v67Dm/wwsTMpxE/7woWo0zlvWCtNgUNiBYtNvsZkmeJifv\nEnSKJU1X3+YEF66l4YiLBRGVQH+g8NsJyQrhLY+5BtkI5EiTr5smbZ6z569alwkH\n4w+ZiqG3D9i9Ds7w2MSrAQqX26dFqVQaXE3W+YJDCDH5bWGrBONJvU3yT9ppyK/o\nS+khGXcmesUeHlQNR3e2hUxzVmzV1vcWmuQF9kdtFflwiF9WozPj2QiE8kBfllrn\n+X8QwBtKCjXFT1c1xXEJ2mu82DHr1ZFpAFY3l8dCOdIWzjbEBIBdfb1yt0ARXihj\n1ykQgTlTlMD6C2PAvpWPHyQ3U7dTjc99Oc4Nl+obuJQCvKf41BuLr/f3pA/z2g5P\nzs9aTm/QNy1681gS9WpCsc85bmcn+CgRMr9DE5P5weIUpdh22imjtOVzpwcaIjuO\naQIqVMogjfy3D2RfhwMd1LHRNM2QB4vVeOyTwSlu0szBjTNFnAvpe1AtAopMJGUY\nUqJlkrFRimZN9w0oIyZN2w/thaMr/5lOImrP06HyK8KQj86dboO7j+9OxJpk5Sqx\n9iFXAcwkjOCp/1lBj/Hv\n=5OoI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T04:12:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https:/