ommit/77b059884e75d81489b20f1a58fdb5b1235c3dab","node_id":"C_kwDOAV7u4doAKDc3YjA1OTg4NGU3NWQ4MTQ4OWIyMGYxYTU4ZmRiNWIxMjM1YzNkYWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commit/0dee899d1f75ccadcbb9d10d26e81812cab16bc9","sha":"0dee899d1f75ccadcbb9d10d26e81812cab16bc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commits/0dee899d1f75ccadcbb9d10d26e81812cab16bc9"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commit/51c0888c97ff80d3e4e34cdffabdca548a163338","sha":"51c0888c97ff80d3e4e34cdffabdca548a163338","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commits/51c0888c97ff80d3e4e34cdffabdca548a163338"}],"sha":"77b059884e75d81489b20f1a58fdb5b1235c3dab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commits/77b059884e75d81489b20f1a58fdb5b1235c3dab"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commits/51c0888c97ff80d3e4e34cdffabdca548a163338/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T15:46:58Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T15:46:58Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"feat: make the library switch usable in the admin\n\nThe setting existed but was not presentable: its labels were not in the\ntranslation files, so every language showed the raw English strings, and the\nhelp text did not say what the setting does or when to switch back.\n\n* Labels and help text translated into all 11 languages.\n* The help text now names the symptoms worth switching back for.\n* README documents both options, states that the states are identical either\n  way, and lists what is worth trying on a real household - grouping, TTS over\n  running playback, favorites, the TV input and a music service search.\n\nVerified that both backends satisfy the whole facade including the music service\naccess, so the switch cannot land on a half-implemented backend.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SEkA4hPRefGNdWC4NaFxWv","tree":{"sha":"3725dd9ce52880568540aff8dd18956274e07d36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/git/trees/3725dd9ce52880568540aff8dd18956274e07d36"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/git/commits/51c0888c97ff80d3e4e34cdffabdca548a163338","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commit/51c0888c97ff80d3e4e34cdffabdca548a163338","node_id":"C_kwDOAV7u4doAKDUxYzA4ODhjOTdmZjgwZDNlNGUzNGNkZmZhYmRjYTU0OGExNjMzMzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commit/be97d369be9835e655ab5de509387237fb8e0239","sha":"be97d369be9835e655ab5de509387237fb8e0239","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commits/be97d369be9835e655ab5de509387237fb8e0239"}],"sha":"51c0888c97ff80d3e4e34cdffabdca548a163338","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commits/51c0888c97ff80d3e4e34cdffabdca548a163338"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commits/be97d369be9835e655ab5de509387237fb8e0239/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T15:39:31Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T15:39:31Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"feat: route browsing and music services through the facade\n\nPhase 4, plus the part of phase 5 that is not a regression.\n\n`main.ts` no longer opens a socket of its own: `browseMedia()`, `hasHomeTheater()`\nand the two SOAP helpers are gone from it, and the count of direct network calls\nin that file is zero. Browsing, the TV probe and the HDMI audio format are device\nmethods now; the music services hang off the backend.\n\n`MediaBrowseItem` and `MediaBrowseResult` moved to `backend/types.ts`. They\ndescribe the domain, not the transport that fetched them; `content-directory.ts`\nre-exports them so nothing else had to change.\n\nBoth backends share `SmapiHub`. The migration analysis assumed it would shrink to\nthe account harvesting, with the library''s `SmapiClient` taking the rest - but\n`SmapiHub` turned out to have no tie to `sonos-discovery` at all, and it can read\nthe accounts a user already linked in the SONOS app out of the speaker, which\n`@svrooij/sonos` documents that it cannot (\"not sure how to fetch this from\nsonos\"). Swapping it in would have lost that, so it stays and is shared.\n\nTwo bugs found while wiring the new backend, both of the kind that only shows up\nagainst real hardware:\n\n* UPnP LastChange events are partial - the speaker sends only what changed. The\n  folding overwrote every field on every event, so an event about the track\n  number reset the transport state to STOPPED and shuffle to off. It is additive\n  now, with seven tests covering it.\n* The transport metadata arrives parsed whenever the library can parse it, so the\n  DIDL string TTS needs to restore radio after an announcement was lost.\n  `MetaDataHelper.TrackToMetaData` puts it back.\n\nPhase 5 stops short of its second half on purpose. Handing the state restore to\n`PlayNotification()` would drop the fade in and fade out the adapter offers, and\nremoving `sonos-discovery` would remove the fallback that makes an alpha without\nhardware testable at all. Both wait until the new backend has been proven.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SEkA4hPRefGNdWC4NaFxWv","tree":{"sha":"9ae5fb8ad4aaa15b21ffafaad97175edf091bf93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/git/trees/9ae5fb8ad4aaa15b21ffafaad97175edf091bf93"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/git/commits/be97d369be9835e655ab5de509387237fb8e0239","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commit/be97d369be9835e655ab5de509387237fb8e0239","node_id":"C_kwDOAV7u4doAKGJlOTdkMzY5YmU5ODM1ZTY1NWFiNWRlNTA5Mzg3MjM3ZmI4ZTAyMzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commit/d531efcadb0896a769901cdf2f42ef970fd93a0f","sha":"d531efcadb0896a769901cdf2f42ef970fd93a0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commits/d531efcadb0896a769901cdf2f42ef970fd93a0f"}],"sha":"be97d369be9835e655ab5de509387237fb8e0239","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commits/be97d369be9835e655ab5de509387237fb8e0239"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commits/d531efcadb0896a769901cdf2f42ef970fd93a0f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T15:23:02Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T15:23:02Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"feat: add the @svrooij/sonos backend behind a config switch\n\nBoth client libraries now ship side by side. `native.backend` picks one, and it\ndefaults to `discovery`, so nothing changes for existing installations.\n\nWithout SONOS hardware here, this switch is what makes an alpha testable: a\ntester who hits a problem flips a setting in the admin instead of downgrading\nthe adapter, and we learn which backend caused it.\n\nThe new backend assembles the state the adapter needs, which the old library\nhanded over ready-made:\n\n* AVTransport events give track, play mode, crossfade and track number.\n* RenderingControl events give volume, mute, bass, treble, night mode and\n  speech enhancement.\n* The play position is not evented at all, so it is read from GetPositionInfo\n  whenever a transport event arrives.\n* Group volume and mute have their own service and are refreshed with the\n  topology, which itself is rebuilt from the per-device coordinator events and\n  only emitted when it actually changed.\n\nShuffle and repeat are one enum in this library but two independent ioBroker\nstates. `toPlayMode`/`fromPlayMode` fold and unfold them; a test walks all six\ncombinations through a round trip, because losing one of them would silently\nbreak existing scripts.\n\n`SonosManager.Devices` throws \"No Devices available!\" until discovery found\nsomething, and the adapter asks for the device list exactly in that situation -\nduring unload, or before the first speaker answers. Every use goes through a\nguarded accessor now.\n\nAlso: `SonosBackend.start()` so both implementations are started the same way,\nand the local address for the TTS files is worked out from the interface that\nshares a subnet with a speaker, which `sonos-discovery` did on its own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SEkA4hPRefGNdWC4NaFxWv","tree":{"sha":"ea9403f4f85df568038449d5cf860a18458612ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/git/trees/ea9403f4f85df568038449d5cf860a18458612ee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/git/commits/d531efcadb0896a769901cdf2f42ef970fd93a0f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commit/d531efcadb0896a769901cdf2f42ef970fd93a0f","node_id":"C_kwDOAV7u4doAKGQ1MzFlZmNhZGIwODk2YTc2OTkwMWNkZjJmNDJlZjk3MGZkOTNhMGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commit/4bd3a0df56b940bb84411e13ea245a4352883780","sha":"4bd3a0df56b940bb84411e13ea245a4352883780","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commits/4bd3a0df56b940bb84411e13ea245a4352883780"}],"sha":"d531efcadb0896a769901cdf2f42ef970fd93a0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commits/d531efcadb0896a769901cdf2f42ef970fd93a0f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commits/4bd3a0df56b940bb84411e13ea245a4352883780/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T14:49:37Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T14:49:37Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"refactor: put a backend facade between the adapter and sonos-discovery\n\nPhase 1 of the migration analysis. No behaviour change - only the boundary moves.\n\n`main.ts` and `lib/tts.ts` no longer know the client library. They talk to\n`SonosBackend` and `SonosDevice` (src/lib/backend), and `discovery-backend.ts`\nis the only file that imports `sonos-discovery`. Swapping the implementation\nlater therefore touches one file instead of 163 call sites.\n\nThe facade also retires three hacks that only existed because the adapter wrote\nonto the library''s player objects:\n\n* `player._address` -> `device.channel` / `device.ip`, computed once per device\n  instead of being patched in at eight different places.\n* `player._volume` / `player._isMuted` -> `device.volume` / `device.muted`.\n  These were never maintained by the library, only by this adapter.\n* `player.tts` -> `Sonos.tts`, a map owned by the adapter.\n\nThe free helpers `getIp()`, `isGroupMember()` and `transportUri()` are gone; the\ndevice answers all three. `toFavoriteList()` is gone too - the backend hands out\narrays, so the array-or-dictionary ambiguity ends at the boundary.\n\nEvents are normalised on the way in, so no object of the library reaches the\nadapter any more:\n\n* `transport-state` carried the player object itself and is reduced to\n  `{ uuid, state }`.\n* `topology-change` carried either the group list or a single device and was\n  told apart by `typeof data.length`; it is now `{ groups }` or `{ uuid }`.\n* `queue` reads the queue in the backend, so every event has the same shape.\n\n`treble` and `bass` stay unsubscribed. sonos-discovery never emits them, the\nhandler in `processSonosEvents` was already an empty documented branch, and\nsubscribing would have been a behaviour change. The backend can deliver them\nonce a backend exists that emits them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SEkA4hPRefGNdWC4NaFxWv","tree":{"sha":"2c12121974310f1768044b7494c6965d06694703","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/git/trees/2c12121974310f1768044b7494c6965d06694703"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/git/commits/4bd3a0df56b940bb84411e13ea245a4352883780","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commit/4bd3a0df56b940bb84411e13ea245a4352883780","node_id":"C_kwDOAV7u4doAKDRiZDNhMGRmNTZiOTQwYmI4NDQxMWUxM2VhMjQ1YTQzNTI4ODM3ODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commit/0dee899d1f75ccadcbb9d10d26e81812cab16bc9","sha":"0dee899d1f75ccadcbb9d10d26e81812cab16bc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commits/0dee899d1f75ccadcbb9d10d26e81812cab16bc9"}],"sha":"4bd3a0df56b940bb84411e13ea245a4352883780","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commits/4bd3a0df56b940bb84411e13ea245a4352883780"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/commits/0dee899d1f75ccadcbb9d10d26e81812cab16bc9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T14:18:57Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T14:18:57Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"chore: release v4.1.0\n\n* (@GermanBluefox) Added a React implementation of `Sonos Control` for vis-2, plus the new `Sonos room` widget\n* (kosmix1980) vis widget: rooms, groups, favorites, playlists, queue, recent tracks and sources\n* (kosmix1980) Sources: TuneIn, music library, network shares, line-in and SMAPI catalog search\n* (kosmix1980) TV HDMI as a playable source with format, cover, night sound and speech enhancement\n* (kosmix1980) Added `playlist_list` / `playlist_list_array` and per-room `recent_tracks`\n* (kosmix1980) Group members follow the coordinator''s now-playing and transport\n* (@GermanBluefox) TV is offered only on speakers that have an HDMI/optical input\n* (@GermanBluefox) Music services are listed only when the household reports them\n* (@GermanBluefox) Removed the YouTube Music catalog search: it used a private, undocumented Google endpoint\n* (@GermanBluefox) Only the group coordinator updates the elapsed time of the group now\n* (@GermanBluefox) SMAPI account tokens are stored with restrictive file permissions","tree":{"sha":"c021ad7831d0fcfe7657755f2d3f49f80bd78fb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/git/trees/c021ad7831d0fcfe7657755f2d3f49f80bd78fb5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.sonos/git/com