m/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/commit/c63750b08943bce2ac75b9876df89fe91e1866ab","node_id":"C_kwDOAWFLbtoAKGM2Mzc1MGIwODk0M2JjZTJhYzc1Yjk4NzZkZjg5ZmU5MWUxODY2YWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/commit/97111eb9a07bf4285651de314b9f8eed031fd95d","sha":"97111eb9a07bf4285651de314b9f8eed031fd95d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/commits/97111eb9a07bf4285651de314b9f8eed031fd95d"}],"sha":"c63750b08943bce2ac75b9876df89fe91e1866ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/commits/c63750b08943bce2ac75b9876df89fe91e1866ab"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/commits/97111eb9a07bf4285651de314b9f8eed031fd95d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T05:32:05Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T05:32:05Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"GUI settings: retry a write that got no answer\n\nA write of the GUI settings that timed out while the connection was up\nkept its changes, but nothing wrote them until the next change. Such a\nwrite is now tried again after 5 seconds; a lost connection is still\nwritten by the reconnect. Also shortened the changelog entry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e9a8f2c4b98e2950758d9440f388bcb8fb57ca7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/git/trees/e9a8f2c4b98e2950758d9440f388bcb8fb57ca7f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/git/commits/97111eb9a07bf4285651de314b9f8eed031fd95d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/commit/97111eb9a07bf4285651de314b9f8eed031fd95d","node_id":"C_kwDOAWFLbtoAKDk3MTExZWI5YTA3YmY0Mjg1NjUxZGUzMTRiOWY4ZWVkMDMxZmQ5NWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/commit/c2e201e9f33a63cefe1c302582cdb4f5b2ec02c8","sha":"c2e201e9f33a63cefe1c302582cdb4f5b2ec02c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/commits/c2e201e9f33a63cefe1c302582cdb4f5b2ec02c8"}],"sha":"97111eb9a07bf4285651de314b9f8eed031fd95d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/commits/97111eb9a07bf4285651de314b9f8eed031fd95d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27220902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krobipd/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krobipd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krobipd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krobipd/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/krobipd","id":27220902,"login":"krobipd","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjIwOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krobipd/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krobipd/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krobipd/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krobipd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krobipd/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/krobipd","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/commits/c2e201e9f33a63cefe1c302582cdb4f5b2ec02c8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T05:28:20Z","email":"krobi@power-dreams.com","name":"krobipd"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T05:28:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"GUI settings: a window no longer throws away what others saved (#3671)\n\nWhen \"store the GUI settings on the server\" is switched on, every open\nadmin window keeps the copy of `system.adapter.admin.0.guiSettings` it\nread when it was opened, and writes that copy back as a whole each time\na setting changes - a column width, an opened folder, the theme.\nWhatever was saved since that window was opened is gone:\n\n- Two windows or devices take each other''s settings away; the last one\nto change something wins.\n- Any other change to the object is undone. On my installation a history\nsetting on this object was switched off, and 16 seconds later the open\nadmin had switched it back on.\n\nThe option exists so that the settings follow the user across browsers\nand devices - exactly the situation in which several windows are open at\nthe same time.\n\n**What changes**\nA window now remembers only what it changed or removed itself. Right\nbefore writing, it reads the object anew, applies just these changes and\nwrites the result. The writes run one after another; the read and the\nwrite each give up after ten seconds without an answer, so a request\nthat never gets one cannot hold back the later writes. A write that\nfails keeps its changes for the next write, and the read after a\nreconnect writes them - before, a dropped connection ended in an\nunhandled rejection and the change was lost.\n\nWhat it does not do: a window still does not see what another window\nsaved until its own next write or a reload, and two writes in the very\nsame moment can still collide in the short gap between the fresh read\nand the write. Before, that gap was the whole time a window was open.\n\n**Verified**\nLocal build on a throwaway js-controller, browser windows driven by\nPlaywright, writing through `window._localStorage` like every component\ndoes:\n\n| Scenario | 8.0.23 | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| a custom setting is switched off after the window read the object,\nthen the window saves a setting | switched back on | stays off |\n| window A and window B each save an entry | only B''s survives | both |\n| B removes its entry | A''s is lost as well | only B''s is gone |\n| the first write is cut by a dropped connection | lost, 3 unhandled\nrejections | written after the reconnect |\n| the read before a write gets no answer for 15 s, a second change\nmeanwhile | both written | both written |\n\n✅ `npm run lint`, `npm run test:package` and `npm run test:integration`\n(incl. the GUI test) are green.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Bluefox <dogafox@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"51554a8b75b0cabc53c4502a7c779a8b52faebd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/git/trees/51554a8b75b0cabc53c4502a7c779a8b52faebd1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/git/commits/c2e201e9f33a63cefe1c302582cdb4f5b2ec02c8","verification":{"payload":"tree 51554a8b75b0cabc53c4502a7c779a8b52faebd1\nparent 060b1e1845e0f4ca221f4725e51932c5c999c369\nauthor krobipd <krobi@power-dreams.com> 1791437300 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791437300 +0200\n\nGUI settings: a window no longer throws away what others saved (#3671)\n\nWhen \"store the GUI settings on the server\" is switched on, every open\nadmin window keeps the copy of `system.adapter.admin.0.guiSettings` it\nread when it was opened, and writes that copy back as a whole each time\na setting changes - a column width, an opened folder, the theme.\nWhatever was saved since that window was opened is gone:\n\n- Two windows or devices take each other''s settings away; the last one\nto change something wins.\n- Any other change to the object is undone. On my installation a history\nsetting on this object was switched off, and 16 seconds later the open\nadmin had switched it back on.\n\nThe option exists so that the settings follow the user across browsers\nand devices - exactly the situation in which several windows are open at\nthe same time.\n\n**What changes**\nA window now remembers only what it changed or removed itself. Right\nbefore writing, it reads the object anew, applies just these changes and\nwrites the result. The writes run one after another; the read and the\nwrite each give up after ten seconds without an answer, so a request\nthat never gets one cannot hold back the later writes. A write that\nfails keeps its changes for the next write, and the read after a\nreconnect writes them - before, a dropped connection ended in an\nunhandled rejection and the change was lost.\n\nWhat it does not do: a window still does not see what another window\nsaved until its own next write or a reload, and two writes in the very\nsame moment can still collide in the short gap between the fresh read\nand the write. Before, that gap was the whole time a window was open.\n\n**Verified**\nLocal build on a throwaway js-controller, browser windows driven by\nPlaywright, writing through `window._localStorage` like every component\ndoes:\n\n| Scenario | 8.0.23 | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| a custom setting is switched off after the window read the object,\nthen the window saves a setting | switched back on | stays off |\n| window A and window B each save an entry | only B''s survives | both |\n| B removes its entry | A''s is lost as well | only B''s is gone |\n| the first write is cut by a dropped connection | lost, 3 unhandled\nrejections | written after the reconnect |\n| the read before a write gets no answer for 15 s, a second change\nmeanwhile | both written | both written |\n\n✅ `npm run lint`, `npm run test:package` and `npm run test:integration`\n(incl. the GUI test) are green.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Bluefox <dogafox@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxyn0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABJgQAHldqXrs16NYEpcCSzvjuask\noob3p+Jsv9e/sE3XfmxQYJLoBp4Bi40eDGYxV44rjS290eE3oaW+ZI39vcMVXEgs\nLAHsCVpY8i0D4isRNzL33EcbjGU6d51uwS/KLaIinczHzAUG2w/whyLhJPh05A2/\nZtiCXOQMjvKsyXrc/mOoFZejOEu1uPE4Z+yPXY3cU1u3fdQyZAVmHjN6OjQb/5K7\nXFIJHFDRHvjw6Pi6IV4fxrnh874rA6Mh608LqJFplRybBDoq9k80nbve2imw3s/k\nNlbVCTJfIvBNn9gBI5mek/0S9lOzA1Kx3ACjIpfFseKZass7yLW60mZ3502yKveL\nm/wjHsuiwlY85Rz7+6FDaITqRa7mZkTJnVrtTQzDo8gTobPlLYeb2kvIXlToBT3X\nWeETWg/6d3arCwmk8xniPOHUTXK50TmXmtOm2HoX37sJ/vpmcBk2S9qMtl8Kzlkx\nO4vIUEMZT9aDt38lMPrIck5K7yvpHQ04WSDOqX/eGWsmdqdIpZWdGPcTOhgTf06U\nhfARG06hKur3AzHrbxTeTtyuTSoH8WgXcc3VqnO4590dRsQKiVdZXPCdwIWIkxpl\nkxRcMfS3t8+e4cQi3yHNT3pHRmDgJjwIkfGBMfXSzUYz0YvvQZNyUgvZuyNAF0LK\n3Hef97yRhtvXqw2DP8YK\n=8BwO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T05:28:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","u