her_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/commit/fefad2ac6ec1e5ce93dd948ef47ae0a8f22a8584","node_id":"C_kwDOAWFLbtoAKGZlZmFkMmFjNmVjMWU1Y2U5M2RkOTQ4ZWY0N2FlMGE4ZjIyYTg1ODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/commit/b0a8298d6f8dc3d693f39ce78d07c69b064fa7d8","sha":"b0a8298d6f8dc3d693f39ce78d07c69b064fa7d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/commits/b0a8298d6f8dc3d693f39ce78d07c69b064fa7d8"}],"sha":"fefad2ac6ec1e5ce93dd948ef47ae0a8f22a8584","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/commits/fefad2ac6ec1e5ce93dd948ef47ae0a8f22a8584"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/commits/b0a8298d6f8dc3d693f39ce78d07c69b064fa7d8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T22:09:20Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T22:09:20Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"chore: release v8.0.21\n\n- (@GermanBluefox) Fixed: on a grown installation, the start of the GUI ran into \"Detected slow connection!\" and the dialog offering a longer read timeout, on a fast local network as well. The start page read the whole object database only to count the objects and the states for its tile - 32 MB on a system with 10,000 objects - which blocked the admin process for seconds, so every other request of the start waited for it and ran into its own timeout. The counting is now done by the server, which answers with two numbers instead (needs `@iobroker/socket-classes` 2.6.0 and `@iobroker/socket-client` 5.4.0; an older backend still reads all objects, but delayed until the start is through). The whole start now transfers 2.4 MB, and the object database is no longer part of it (#3656)\n- (@GermanBluefox) Fixed: the news check read all objects a second time, right after the start page had read them\n- (@GermanBluefox) Fixed: the admin stayed on its logo and only came up after the page was reloaded. The start reads its own settings, the easy mode and the GUI settings one after the other, and each of them with a timeout of five seconds - which is less than a busy host needs for the first requests. Those reads no longer end the start, and whatever else goes wrong, the app is shown instead of the loader: the menu, the error message and the reconnect are more use than a logo that never goes away (#3641)\n- (@GermanBluefox) Changed: the read timeout starts at 30 seconds instead of 15 (60 instead of 40 in the cloud), and it now applies to every request of the start instead of only to the repository and the installed versions\n- (@GermanBluefox) Changed: the dialog about a slow connection only appears for a read the user asked for - switching the host or retrying from the dialog itself. Nothing waits for the read of the start any more, so a dialog there interrupted a start that was going perfectly well otherwise\n- (@GermanBluefox) Added: the \"Resource usage\" card has a button that first stops the recording of CPU and RAM by the history instance, then collapses the card, which gives the system log room for 16 lines instead of 6. A collapsed card reads nothing at all until it is opened again, and it stays collapsed after a reload (needs `@iobroker/gui-components` 10.3.7)\n- (@GermanBluefox) Fixed: a timeout while reading `guiSettings` at the start overwrote the stored GUI settings of the user with the defaults\n- (@GermanBluefox) Fixed: the system log of the start page was left empty by \"Cannot get logs: TypeError: e.pop is not a function\" when the host answered with anything but its log lines","tree":{"sha":"13090d15b6d2a4145a7039f67e1aedd918a51777","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/git/trees/13090d15b6d2a4145a7039f67e1aedd918a51777"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/git/commits/b0a8298d6f8dc3d693f39ce78d07c69b064fa7d8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gi