avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27220902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krobipd/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krobipd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krobipd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krobipd/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/krobipd","id":27220902,"login":"krobipd","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjIwOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krobipd/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krobipd/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krobipd/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krobipd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krobipd/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/krobipd","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/commits/346048805d7356ae1c90afa81d8e79715a399ce0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T19:40:10Z","email":"krobi@power-dreams.com","name":"krobipd"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T19:40:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Start does not wait for the repository of the host (#3647)\n\n### What the user sees\n\nOpening the admin shows the start screen with the ioBroker logo for\nabout half a minute, then everything appears at once. It happens on\nevery installation whose host cannot reach the repository server\nquickly: no internet access, a firewall in between, or simply a slow\nrepository.\n\n### What it costs, measured\n\nA local ioBroker whose host does not reach the repository, admin 8.0.17,\nPlaywright, time from opening `#tab-objects` until the first row of the\ntable:\n\n| | master | this branch |\n|---|---|---|\n| until the first row | **31.2 s** | **1.1 s** |\n\nRecording the websocket traffic shows where the time goes: every request\nof the start is answered within 0.7 s, each in a few milliseconds. Then\nnothing happens for 30 seconds. Two requests never get an answer —\n`getCompactRepository` (sent at 0.64 s) and `getCompactInstalled` (sent\nat 15.6 s) — and each of them runs into its own read timeout of 15\nseconds, one after the other.\n\n### Why it happens\n\n`readRepoAndInstalledInfo` reads three things — the repository, the\ninstalled versions and the adapters — and awaits them **one after the\nother**, so their read timeouts add up. And `onReady` awaits that whole\nfunction **before** it sets `ready`, so the admin keeps showing its\nloader until the last timeout has elapsed. Only the adapters tab needs\nthose three; the menu, the objects, the logs and everything else are\nready without them.\n\n### What this PR does\n\n- The three reads run at the same time (`Promise.all`) instead of in a\nrow. Each keeps its own error handling exactly as before, including the\n\"slow connection\" warning on a timeout.\n- The start does not wait for them any more. They fill the same state as\nbefore, whenever their answers arrive — so the adapters tab shows its\ndata as soon as the host delivers it, and everything else is usable\nimmediately.\n\nNothing else changes: a host that answers quickly delivers the same data\nat practically the same moment as before, and the other callers of\n`readRepoAndInstalledInfo` (host switch, repository update, the reload\nafter an installation) keep awaiting it as they did.\n\n### Verified\n\n- ✅ `npm run lint`, `cd src-admin && npm run check-ts`, `npm run build`,\n`npm test`, `npm run test:gui` on Node 22\n- ✅ The measurement above, run against the same local ioBroker in both\ndirections, with the websocket traffic recorded: the two requests are\nstill unanswered with this change — the admin simply no longer waits for\nthem\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Bluefox <dogafox@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"b0571a7ddc63dcee12fa5d0809fd591781fdadb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/git/trees/b0571a7ddc63dcee12fa5d0809fd591781fdadb6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/git/commits/346048805d7356ae1c90afa81d8e79715a399ce0","verification":{"payload":"tree b0571a7ddc63dcee12fa5d0809fd591781fdadb6\nparent 849ff272f2712f2b7d341ee00a9f6ae86317ee15\nauthor krobipd <krobi@power-dreams.com> 1790106010 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790106010 +0200\n\nStart does not wait for the repository of the host (#3647)\n\n### What the user sees\n\nOpening the admin shows the start screen with the ioBroker logo for\nabout half a minute, then everything appears at once. It happens on\nevery installation whose host cannot reach the repository server\nquickly: no internet access, a firewall in between, or simply a slow\nrepository.\n\n### What it costs, measured\n\nA local ioBroker whose host does not reach the repository, admin 8.0.17,\nPlaywright, time from opening `#tab-objects` until the first row of the\ntable:\n\n| | master | this branch |\n|---|---|---|\n| until the first row | **31.2 s** | **1.1 s** |\n\nRecording the websocket traffic shows where the time goes: every request\nof the start is answered within 0.7 s, each in a few milliseconds. Then\nnothing happens for 30 seconds. Two requests never get an answer —\n`getCompactRepository` (sent at 0.64 s) and `getCompactInstalled` (sent\nat 15.6 s) — and each of them runs into its own read timeout of 15\nseconds, one after the other.\n\n### Why it happens\n\n`readRepoAndInstalledInfo` reads three things — the repository, the\ninstalled versions and the adapters — and awaits them **one after the\nother**, so their read timeouts add up. And `onReady` awaits that whole\nfunction **before** it sets `ready`, so the admin keeps showing its\nloader until the last timeout has elapsed. Only the adapters tab needs\nthose three; the menu, the objects, the logs and everything else are\nready without them.\n\n### What this PR does\n\n- The three reads run at the same time (`Promise.all`) instead of in a\nrow. Each keeps its own error handling exactly as before, including the\n\"slow connection\" warning on a timeout.\n- The start does not wait for them any more. They fill the same state as\nbefore, whenever their answers arrive — so the adapters tab shows its\ndata as soon as the host delivers it, and everything else is usable\nimmediately.\n\nNothing else changes: a host that answers quickly delivers the same data\nat practically the same moment as before, and the other callers of\n`readRepoAndInstalledInfo` (host switch, repository update, the reload\nafter an installation) keep awaiting it as they did.\n\n### Verified\n\n- ✅ `npm run lint`, `cd src-admin && npm run check-ts`, `npm run build`,\n`npm test`, `npm run test:gui` on Node 22\n- ✅ The measurement above, run against the same local ioBroker in both\ndirections, with the websocket traffic recorded: the two requests are\nstill unanswered with this change — the admin simply no longer waits for\nthem\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Bluefox <dogafox@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqstmbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqIoQAISRz5x2sWPxHxYJ3p7KtGgz\nFQEMu9rkbmPtkYe2Tpwa1nT8oAEwssl8v/QKaUlviTPMcrpZdV+ZkR5ixZpbMH4S\nGLf+AuBA1CwSwG9zmY1iwsPONHE0dCKarXxFbi4/CZNtbL/Syj2Pd6bGA5o4gM1X\nmqRnJFv7hy01yFYb+c5JctDZM2Iz5Z3EfSqwAksIgESOM3yn2LsK/1i2gZdCtdgZ\nNH37/yvA1ZlwQGTRD+Jf0u6i5IymX2tY5Hc+QZ57++ky/0LxVIMmjW1yJwYCvQMI\nZBdvOUvqKk/IMb0QbfIu44VOOPTYrm1ELRgrDvrWtck9BsxgQcMAuF7XjIk6pxt8\nK6stDEmYSUuKLJOb4MeWuREzEqRFy4XfuBY46/e9xGVnmlPimyKzxDrOX/P3Q3yA\nfd2awMXSEPPPfOu1KSfOEvKPThh73wLOHAG4uGuVKeGOde4buJJfphWKKxl7RfYE\nx5qVsGoU6kbmQiKG9QWVWC++SH7JlWo6UvFiIB94npP+dpmy/eibEa1NIwJaRx0Q\nOH96woGPn91xhwuro