https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/commits/0f3d8c71d8242d7b257c2400aad7d97adeb3d008/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T10:27:27Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T10:27:27Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"feat: hand the admin''s own Ace editor to @iobroker/json-config 10.x\n\nNot my work: this was already in the working tree, finished, with its changelog\nentry written. Committed here because it was asked for, and on its own rather\nthan mixed into the Python change beside it.\n\njson-config 10 no longer brings `react-ace`, so the admin passes its editor in\nthrough the new `AceEditor` property. Until now every custom component of every\nadapter carried the whole `ace-builds` in its bundle, although only three of the\nsixty controls ever show an editor. The modes and themes move into a local\n`AceEditor` component, and `Editor.tsx` imports that instead of importing them\none by one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015McHmTR6q5oWNfBsvtkcui","tree":{"sha":"93ca55ae576150ef2fb32a1afc8d4497f1aa861a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/git/trees/93ca55ae576150ef2fb32a1afc8d4497f1aa861a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/git/commits/0f3d8c71d8242d7b257c2400aad7d97adeb3d008","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/user