vents","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.javascript/commits/a2e1ce506493f0afdcf1141ef391fff71014a42b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:04:45Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:04:45Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"The reasoning of an OpenAI-compatible endpoint was switched off unconditionally","tree":{"sha":"e3d15fc9a0628a3e01544e94836f9d2fda5a6330","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.javascript/git/trees/e3d15fc9a0628a3e01544e94836f9d2fda5a6330"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.javascript/git/commits/a2e1ce506493f0afdcf1141ef391fff71014a42b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.javascript/commit/a2e1ce506493f0afdcf1141ef391fff71014a42b","node_id":"C_kwDOAWFL2NoAKGEyZTFjZTUwNjQ5M2YwYWZkY2YxMTQxZWYzOTFmZmY3MTAxNGE0MmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.javascript/commit/793ba326da1c7e4421c9f27c0c6dd40eb160f207","sha":"793ba326da1c7e4421c9f27c0c6dd40eb160f207","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.javascript/commits/793ba326da1c7e4421c9f27c0c6dd40eb160f207"}],"sha":"a2e1ce506493f0afdcf1141ef391fff71014a42b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.javascript/commits/a2e1ce506493f0afdcf1141ef391fff71014a42b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176587999?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foxbot76/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foxbot76/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foxbot76/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foxbot76/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/foxbot76","id":176587999,"login":"foxbot76","node_id":"U_kgDOCoaE3w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foxbot76/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foxbot76/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foxbot76/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foxbot76/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foxbot76/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/foxbot76","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.javascript/commits/793ba326da1c7e4421c9f27c0c6dd40eb160f207/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T21:36:09Z","email":"heusinger.moritz@gmail.com","name":"foxbot76"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T21:36:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[OFFICIAL RELEASE] 10.1.4\n\n* (@GermanBluefox) Rules: the text of an action can round the trigger value with `%.1s` - any number of digits after the decimal point, also `%.2old` for the old value - formatted with the decimal separator of the system, so `Kühlschrank zu warm (%.1s°C)` gives `29,4°C` where `%s` gave `29.400000000000002°C`\n* (@GermanBluefox) Corrected the function block in blockly\n* (@GermanBluefox) A custom OpenAI-compatible AI endpoint answered \"Invalid API key\" in the inline completion and while loading the model list, although the test button in the settings said \"ok\": both asked the adapter for the provider `openai`, and the adapter picks the key by that name, so they used the \"OpenAI API key\" instead of the \"Custom API key\". The custom endpoint is now addressed as what it is, everywhere (#2369)\n* (@GermanBluefox) A configured \"Custom API Base URL\" also redirected every request meant for OpenAI itself to that address - with the OpenAI key attached and no way to switch it off. The base URL now belongs to the custom endpoint alone, so both can be used side by side. If the key of your custom endpoint is in the \"OpenAI API key\" field, move it to the \"Custom API key\" field; the adapter writes a warning in the log if it finds such a setup (#2369)","tree":{"sha":"1725ad359f3fc4397839245d6169f0747786c136","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.javascript/git/trees/1725ad359f3fc4397839245d6169f0747786c136"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.javascript/git/commits/793ba326da1c7e4421c9f27c0c6dd40eb160f207","verification":{"payload":"tree 1725ad359f3fc4397839245d6169f0747786c136\nparent 9b41145764c59955817aa760d360b5b2f96f680f\nauthor foxbot76 <heusinger.moritz@gmail.com> 1788471369 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788471369 +0000\n\n[OFFICIAL RELEASE] 10.1.4\n\n* (@GermanBluefox) Rules: the text of an action can round the trigger value with `%.1s` - any number of digits after the decimal point, also `%.2old` for the old value - formatted with the decimal separator of the system, so `Kühlschrank zu warm (%.1s°C)` gives `29,4°C` where `%s` gave `29.400000000000002°C`\n* (@GermanBluefox) Corrected the function block in blockly\n* (@GermanBluefox) A custom OpenAI-compatible AI endpoint answered \"Invalid API key\" in the inline completion and while loading the model list, although the test button in the settings said \"ok\": both asked the adapter for the provider `openai`, and the adapter picks the key by that name, so they used the \"OpenAI API key\" instead of the \"Custom API key\". The custom endpoint is now addressed as what it is, everywhere (#2369)\n* (@GermanBluefox) A configured \"Custom API Base URL\" also redirected every request meant for OpenAI itself to that address - with the OpenAI key attached and no way to switch it off. The base URL now belongs to the custom endpoint alone, so both can be used side by side. If the key of your custom endpoint is in the \"OpenAI API key\" field, move it to the \"Custom API key\" field; the adapter writes a warning in the log if it finds such a setup (#2369)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmehJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjLoQALIS77j89tZkzeryF2BCk3fR\nbax1cj8YIQmv8KTiC1jYiQJtxLu/Rg5/82XKsUSCnK6f+3zcpfF0KncF+mAuCJDL\nImbmiB/i0G+37hk3JusIl8b7rhXE+zdXIngGQe10p3qvOg54IAf1MXNsJd0iMqKE\n4ROQANDFP8pI0W5gA0qE2BUsS0xXX9YUPJ3RPyMAJZzHrvLmPIpeP33P38EQbUs0\n6A0am9YbqJ+xKMlVXZvBzZzNoso46FsI9PJrptsu+4dPQmIXKbBiCzKZpXMWPCcl\neuvxRtS3iv3HvjEkU16LYU85GrP6PZ3Lz9zghBqRbK7YGOau5E5KJMLi9V8pa0BY\nXTGPw9jjmJS5ajvox9Edm7VKjiFA9pPW1vyKmt9M40ov/XaWirAUykuutcD8A9A6\nlH9xyQAXkxg3wdVWlIFuouATmZ7yLECMwGvz/cTYS6PfH7HBhKezhAtexAGm7WhC\n43yzVWpmE1wRuOVsePxRpzN7KGlPEPjOGyYdAN9GYaYkNUO+mB5BWvEuB3KKORGZ\neg6JFTADKLqUsFo4Ldh+fXvC7GVJ4NR8UDjARehOy6xb/Q4HOKmW6O869nAc16xP\nrRXM2s1jrQkgoD5+vTC