l":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.javascript/commit/278fa8f7a195dca869bbede751dfc494336d2387","node_id":"C_kwDOAWFL2NoAKDI3OGZhOGY3YTE5NWRjYTg2OWJiZWRlNzUxZGZjNDk0MzM2ZDIzODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.javascript/commit/2eff8e12cdfcc6547cea9d0e58a6fad3e3b55b9e","sha":"2eff8e12cdfcc6547cea9d0e58a6fad3e3b55b9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.javascript/commits/2eff8e12cdfcc6547cea9d0e58a6fad3e3b55b9e"}],"sha":"278fa8f7a195dca869bbede751dfc494336d2387","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.javascript/commits/278fa8f7a195dca869bbede751dfc494336d2387"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1881217?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eistee82/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eistee82/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eistee82/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eistee82/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Eistee82","id":1881217,"login":"Eistee82","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4ODEyMTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eistee82/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eistee82/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eistee82/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eistee82/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eistee82/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eistee82","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.javascript/commits/2eff8e12cdfcc6547cea9d0e58a6fad3e3b55b9e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T17:56:32Z","email":"Eistee82@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Eistee"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T17:56:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: VS-Code-style AI assistant in the JavaScript editor (#2222)\n\nAdds a polished AI experience inside the script editor, expands the\nprovider story, and adds a custom-base-URL key alongside the encrypted\nkey storage merged from upstream #2205.\n\nEditor experience\n- Code-lens row above each function/class/arrow with Explain / Refactor / Tests\n- Inline chat widget (Alt+I) for quick prompts on a selection\n- Monaco hover shows live ioBroker state info (value, type, role, room)\n- Datapoint autocomplete in getState/setState/on/$ patterns\n- VS-Code-style inline diff with Apply/Discard toolbar in its own view-zone\n- Smart Show-Diff fallback that targets the matching block in the script\n- Slash commands and context-menu entries mirror the code-lens actions\n\nAI provider improvements\n- Native Anthropic tool-calling support for Claude models\n- Provider resolver with custom base-URL key (Ollama, LM Studio, etc.)\n- 10 Monaco editor tools the AI agent can drive\n- Mode tooltip explains Agent vs Ask vs Edit use cases\n- Non-chat model filter expanded with observed and Ollama-library models\n- Inline chat returns explanations rather than echoing the selection\n- Code blocks honor leading JSDoc and stop at the matching closing brace\n\nSecurity\n- Adds gptBaseUrlKey to encryptedNative + protectedNative + native, on top\n  of the existing keys merged from upstream #2205 (gptKey, claudeKey,\n  geminiKey, deepseekKey)\n- Removed unsupported ''placeholder'' on password fields (W5512)\n- Subtle row tinting + accent rail in chat to distinguish user vs AI;\n  Avatar foreground uses theme.palette.getContrastText so the icon stays\n  readable in both themes\n\nTests & docs\n- Vitest suites for code-lens provider, prompt builder, applyCodeEdit,\n  editor tools, find-AI-block-target, inline chat widget, inline diff\n  controller, isChatModel, objectMatchesQuery, state hover provider\n- Backend integration tests for AI provider resolver and Anthropic adapter\n- Translations for all 11 languages updated\n- Changelog entries under WORK IN PROGRESS\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3619fa6da15767565028db93b457fc0f9beac55f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.javascript/git/trees/3619fa6da15767565028db93b457fc0f9beac55f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.javascript/git/commits/2eff8e12cdfcc6547cea9d0e58a6fad3e3b55b9e","verification":{"payload":"tree 3619fa6da15767565028db93b457fc0f9beac55f\nparent c68a69838cf51d5e5b08f9c77f197eea466500ab\nauthor Eistee <Eistee82@users.noreply.github.com> 1777571792 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777571792 +0200\n\nfeat: VS-Code-style AI assistant in the JavaScript editor (#2222)\n\nAdds a polished AI experience inside the script editor, expands the\nprovider story, and adds a custom-base-URL key alongside the encrypted\nkey storage merged from upstream #2205.\n\nEditor experience\n- Code-lens row above each function/class/arrow with Explain / Refactor / Tests\n- Inline chat widget (Alt+I) for quick prompts on a selection\n- Monaco hover shows live ioBroker state info (value, type, role, room)\n- Datapoint autocomplete in getState/setState/on/$ patterns\n- VS-Code-style inline diff with Apply/Discard toolbar in its own view-zone\n- Smart Show-Diff fallback that targets the matching block in the script\n- Slash commands and context-menu entries mirror the code-lens actions\n\nAI provider improvements\n- Native Anthropic tool-calling support for Claude models\n- Provider resolver with custom base-URL key (Ollama, LM Studio, etc.)\n- 10 Monaco editor tools the AI agent can drive\n- Mode tooltip explains Agent vs Ask vs Edit use cases\n- Non-chat model filter expanded with observed and Ollama-library models\n- Inline chat returns explanations rather than echoing the selection\n- Code blocks honor leading JSDoc and stop at the matching closing brace\n\nSecurity\n- Adds gptBaseUrlKey to encryptedNative + protectedNative + native, on top\n  of the existing keys merged from upstream #2205 (gptKey, claudeKey,\n  geminiKey, deepseekKey)\n- Removed unsupported ''placeholder'' on password fields (W5512)\n- Subtle row tinting + accent rail in chat to distinguish user vs AI;\n  Avatar foreground uses theme.palette.getContrastText so the icon stays\n  readable in both themes\n\nTests & docs\n- Vitest suites for code-lens provider, prompt builder, applyCodeEdit,\n  editor tools, find-AI-block-target, inline chat widget, inline diff\n  controller, isChatModel, objectMatchesQuery, state hover provider\n- Backend integration tests for AI provider resolver and Anthropic adapter\n- Translations for all 11 languages updated\n- Changelog entries under WORK IN PROGRESS\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp85fQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2N0QAF0eHvHazvUKs7+fQpF860Jb\nBur1d2WNusyOnPzO1Xaq9v+1zpST6vGI/+h8Ana1ScX4U6OzZUbjo6TZRFdO681Z\nJko1sYVexTy3WsKeON4gpGgbP+B85jF4IKpcSz5F6W/rN7vtHGdlJCMUVYmUlQQD\nMBDirwcTlneK3c14E2u8wmIhXLgSel6dE2PAiW4fCAgMlXQgvRh4Won+OPD/EjhD\nZewgnLu5TDwq60Oz73eK7H2OHR1sI0Q3u0Yjl+K5E2l/bWYldPaUT+bQ5dHZOBjy\nqU0b+Cd3okUe9PFuI7S6hFQtU9ekVouV7Va3IrmjrSh1qAN0x3COnWnW3Po0pxTj\nYmztJo14T9w2jW3JO8MMRP5OmdOCX34k3tzwg0KZFO2hgNLs0SkR7Apzt4nDHwon\ntkFR61GxAlYnYBSDBU9rTHdxvUVGB1pGPDVZ3SpV0UmFaB9qzqK5956OQXvFIT33\n02BkzgggrdHtR2emryw3ev63vViwr+dQ8biHMkRieVssHi40KdHd2dW9/pl5KIJZ\nf+j0Z5uRb3HmWZWGRq/xPCDdcem9TArt4z+NX5R1fT9b8k6Blnyln9YpiB6nZTTD\nZhQI5HYy++/NgPWId8msTr9o2Pm26zH7f0xrdy/KvYM3UWgVtQj4Z4WD+IIXXrBy\n6qbwD0WiI65xBYRq5bbz\n=ZG80\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-30T17:56:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https: