n\n* fix: render the identity-provider administration screen only for server administrators\n\n* docs: reword the permission comments to state the rule, not the failure mode\n\nReview feedback on the equivalent change in module-manager (#199): the comments explained too much\nabout what goes wrong without the requirement, which is more than a public repository should carry.\nReworded to the framing agreed there — state the design rule (\"a component''s access rule should travel\nwith the component and hold on every render path, regardless of where it is placed\") and the reason for\nthe permission chosen, and drop the description of what happens when it is absent.\n\nComment-only; no behaviour change.","tree":{"sha":"301c8750897f9f8a60b64b5f27524b1b512debba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/external-provider-users-groups/git/trees/301c8750897f9f8a60b64b5f27524b1b512debba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/external-provider-users-groups/git/commits/80c971af71df0ed423abe32d5245b8c17f4eeb96","verification":{"payload":"tree 301c8750897f9f8a60b64b5f27524b1b512debba\nparent d812717f6f9ba00ff29cace19cbf40ce09d33b40\nauthor Alex Karmanov <alexandrk_@hotmail.com> 1785935551 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785935551 -0400\n\nfix: render the identity-provider administration screen only for server administrators (#122)\n\n* fix: render the identity-provider administration screen only for server administrators\n\n* docs: reword the permission comments to state the rule, not the failure mode\n\nReview feedback on the equivalent change in module-manager (#199): the comments explained too much\nabout what goes wrong without the requirement, which is more than a public repository should carry.\nReworded to the framing agreed there — state the design rule (\"a component''s access rule should travel\nwith the component and hold on every render path, regardless of where it is placed\") and the reason for\nthe permission chosen, and drop the description o